1
00:00:00,293 --> 00:00:01,861
The score is 23 to 24.

2
00:00:01,861 --> 00:00:04,130
It's set point for the Red Sparks
in the first set.

3
00:00:05,265 --> 00:00:07,234
We need to cover! Cover!

4
00:00:07,601 --> 00:00:10,804
Jin, look out for the middle. It's open.

5
00:00:11,304 --> 00:00:13,640
(The goal is to back attack.)

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,008
Serve!

7
00:00:16,977 --> 00:00:17,945
Sorry.

8
00:00:18,411 --> 00:00:19,545
No, go!

9
00:00:19,713 --> 00:00:20,547
Sorry.

10
00:00:21,147 --> 00:00:23,850
(Hye In sets the ball well,)

11
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:26,052
(and Jin passes it to the back.)

12
00:00:30,557 --> 00:00:32,425
- Enkhsoyol.
- It's out!

13
00:00:32,592 --> 00:00:33,526
It's out.

14
00:00:37,163 --> 00:00:39,932
And just like that,
the first set comes to an end.

15
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:42,035
The score is 23 to 25.

16
00:00:42,168 --> 00:00:44,804
The first set goes to the Red Sparks.

17
00:00:45,538 --> 00:00:48,474
(The opponent takes the first set.)

18
00:00:48,708 --> 00:00:52,078
(Second set pre-tactic timeout)

19
00:00:53,513 --> 00:00:54,447
Let's have a look.

20
00:00:54,447 --> 00:00:56,749
(Checking the first set score sheet)

21
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,151
Look at Seung Ju.

22
00:01:00,153 --> 00:01:03,857
(Seung Ju's attack efficiency is
only 14 percent.)

23
00:01:03,957 --> 00:01:07,727
The opposing players played with Seung Ju
for who knows how many hours.

24
00:01:07,727 --> 00:01:09,662
So none of Seung Ju's attacks are working.

25
00:01:09,662 --> 00:01:12,398
But we don't have anyone
to substitute at this point.

26
00:01:13,266 --> 00:01:15,835
If Chae Rim were here,
we could've sent her in.

27
00:01:15,835 --> 00:01:18,304
(The absence of the teammates feels
even bigger today.)

28
00:01:18,805 --> 00:01:22,776
I also felt that my performance wasn't
great.

29
00:01:23,276 --> 00:01:25,979
I really want to do well,
but it's not working out.

30
00:01:26,179 --> 00:01:27,747
That makes me lose my confidence.

31
00:01:27,981 --> 00:01:31,185
So I wondered how I could overcome that.

32
00:01:31,185 --> 00:01:32,819
I kept having these thoughts.

33
00:01:33,753 --> 00:01:36,756
(Sighing)

34
00:01:37,657 --> 00:01:38,658
Seung Ju can't attack,

35
00:01:38,658 --> 00:01:39,993
so maybe we can switch her with Tamira.

36
00:01:39,993 --> 00:01:41,828
And Enkhsoyol can receive.

37
00:01:42,429 --> 00:01:43,330
What do you think?

38
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:49,169
(Tamira going on court as a substitution
in the second set?)

39
00:01:49,402 --> 00:01:52,338
But I think she'll be confused
about defense positions...

40
00:01:52,338 --> 00:01:53,472
when she moves around on the court.

41
00:01:53,707 --> 00:01:54,574
You think so?

42
00:01:54,574 --> 00:01:58,445
And I'm concerned
about the errors she made in the past.

43
00:01:59,679 --> 00:02:03,349
(Every time she was sent in
as a substitution...)

44
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:05,519
(Come on, Tamira.)

45
00:02:06,086 --> 00:02:11,525
(she had shaky defense.)

46
00:02:13,793 --> 00:02:15,862
Tamira!

47
00:02:15,862 --> 00:02:19,366
The ball was right there!

48
00:02:21,001 --> 00:02:22,702
- We're just stuck.
- We are.

49
00:02:22,702 --> 00:02:24,270
(Thinking)

50
00:02:25,438 --> 00:02:28,074
(They've decided
to trust Seung Ju for now.)

51
00:02:28,074 --> 00:02:28,808
It's okay.

52
00:02:29,175 --> 00:02:30,777
Let's have a review.

53
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:32,144
What was our problem?

54
00:02:32,479 --> 00:02:34,748
Eight to zero at the beginning?
What was that?

55
00:02:34,948 --> 00:02:38,218
If not for that, we would've gotten
way more points and had an easier game.

56
00:02:38,351 --> 00:02:41,621
We started off with eight to zero
and still had a tough game.

57
00:02:41,621 --> 00:02:42,489
Seriously?

58
00:02:42,589 --> 00:02:45,024
You hit a few sloppy ones,
and the flow is ruined.

59
00:02:45,024 --> 00:02:46,692
We just need a strong start.
Everything else was fine.

60
00:02:46,693 --> 00:02:48,061
- We weren't bad.
- Yes, Coach.

61
00:02:48,061 --> 00:02:49,963
- Red Sparks!
- Let's go!

62
00:02:50,296 --> 00:02:51,831
- One, two, three! Let's go!
- Let's go!

63
00:02:52,098 --> 00:02:53,666
- Let's do this!
- Let's go!

64
00:02:53,666 --> 00:02:55,468
The first set was very disappointing.

65
00:02:55,468 --> 00:02:56,970
It was 23 to 25.

66
00:02:56,970 --> 00:02:59,039
The Red Sparks took the set.

67
00:02:59,239 --> 00:03:03,109
Enkhsoyol scored 7 points
with a 47 percent attack success rate.

68
00:03:03,309 --> 00:03:06,112
But it's been tough on Seung Ju.

69
00:03:06,112 --> 00:03:09,282
Right. Just until a few months ago,
she and the Red Sparks players...

70
00:03:09,282 --> 00:03:10,984
practiced together.

71
00:03:10,984 --> 00:03:13,386
They always watched each other play,

72
00:03:13,686 --> 00:03:16,155
so Seung Ju's plays are not
working out well.

73
00:03:16,656 --> 00:03:19,726
(Second set, Red Sparks 0 : Wonder Dogs 0)

74
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:22,329
(First serve, Da Bin)

75
00:03:22,896 --> 00:03:24,097
It's a drop serve!

76
00:03:26,232 --> 00:03:28,601
Left side. Watch for the left side.

77
00:03:28,601 --> 00:03:29,869
The second set is starting.

78
00:03:32,305 --> 00:03:33,907
My ball. Come on, Jin.

79
00:03:33,907 --> 00:03:34,974
(Shaky reception)

80
00:03:34,974 --> 00:03:36,509
- Go!
- Hit it!

81
00:03:36,509 --> 00:03:37,910
- Go!
- Enkhsoyol.

82
00:03:37,911 --> 00:03:39,212
(Whistle blowing)

83
00:03:39,479 --> 00:03:40,980
(Point for Red Sparks?)

84
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,782
That's a four-hit violation.

85
00:03:44,384 --> 00:03:46,486
(After Seung Ju and Jin,)

86
00:03:47,253 --> 00:03:50,423
(Enkhsoyol's spike hits the net...)

87
00:03:50,423 --> 00:03:52,925
(and Song Hee passed it,
which was the fourth hit.)

88
00:03:55,061 --> 00:03:56,596
My bad.

89
00:03:56,596 --> 00:03:57,564
My mistake.

90
00:03:57,564 --> 00:03:58,932
Seung Ju,

91
00:03:58,932 --> 00:04:00,600
step in closer. This is our free ball.

92
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:01,968
- Yes, Coach.
- Step in.

93
00:04:02,969 --> 00:04:04,604
Everyone, just step in. Don't kneel down.

94
00:04:04,604 --> 00:04:05,805
(Sighing)

95
00:04:06,072 --> 00:04:07,907
(The game continues)

96
00:04:08,141 --> 00:04:10,543
- Hit it!
- Eun Ji spikes!

97
00:04:14,814 --> 00:04:17,617
(We knew you had it!)

98
00:04:17,617 --> 00:04:19,352
Nice spike, Eun Ji!

99
00:04:20,053 --> 00:04:23,356
Eun Ji's attacks are breaking
through the Wonder Dogs' defense.

100
00:04:23,356 --> 00:04:25,091
During the first set,

101
00:04:25,091 --> 00:04:27,927
Eun Ji had a 50 percent success rate
and scored 8 points.

102
00:04:29,262 --> 00:04:34,734
(She scored the first point
of the first set...)

103
00:04:35,268 --> 00:04:38,738
(and hit wonderful spikes
at every crucial moment.)

104
00:04:39,706 --> 00:04:44,277
(She'd been the Wonder Dogs' worst enemy
during the whole first set.)

105
00:04:44,777 --> 00:04:47,446
(Ace Eun Ji)

106
00:04:48,047 --> 00:04:51,584
Hyeon Jeong, don't just rush
over at the end.

107
00:04:51,818 --> 00:04:54,587
How many times have I said so?

108
00:04:55,722 --> 00:04:57,991
(Ye Rim's service)

109
00:04:58,358 --> 00:04:59,259
Serve!

110
00:05:01,227 --> 00:05:02,728
No!

111
00:05:03,029 --> 00:05:03,963
Jin.

112
00:05:04,664 --> 00:05:05,598
Spike!

113
00:05:05,765 --> 00:05:06,666
Oh, crap!

114
00:05:07,167 --> 00:05:07,934
My ball!
(Back to attack again)

115
00:05:08,868 --> 00:05:10,036
Let's stay calm.

116
00:05:10,036 --> 00:05:11,237
(Enkhsoyol attacking)

117
00:05:11,237 --> 00:05:14,140
Enkhsoyol feint-tips! And it works!

118
00:05:15,308 --> 00:05:17,610
(She can switch between tips
and spikes freely now.)

119
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:19,579
- Good job.
- Nice.

120
00:05:20,613 --> 00:05:22,081
- Seo Hyun!
- Yes?

121
00:05:22,081 --> 00:05:24,150
- It's your job to defend that.
- Okay, Coach.

122
00:05:24,150 --> 00:05:26,119
- Don't miss it next time, okay?
- Yes, Coach.

123
00:05:26,586 --> 00:05:27,487
Eun Ji.

124
00:05:28,154 --> 00:05:29,722
(Message received)

125
00:05:30,256 --> 00:05:31,924
(Now at a tie)

126
00:05:31,924 --> 00:05:33,159
The score is tied at two.

127
00:05:33,159 --> 00:05:34,827
(Song Hee's serve)

128
00:05:34,827 --> 00:05:35,861
Song Hee is serving.

129
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:40,300
It hit the net!

130
00:05:40,533 --> 00:05:41,634
They passed it.

131
00:05:41,734 --> 00:05:42,568
Hit it!

132
00:05:43,102 --> 00:05:44,870
A tip, but it's blocked.

133
00:05:45,371 --> 00:05:46,272
Going the other way.

134
00:05:46,272 --> 00:05:47,273
(Eun Ji's attack)

135
00:05:47,273 --> 00:05:48,341
Hit it!

136
00:05:51,077 --> 00:05:53,246
The ball is set high, and Jin chases.

137
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:55,281
Nice toss.

138
00:05:55,281 --> 00:05:56,249
Chase the ball.

139
00:05:56,716 --> 00:05:57,784
Enkhsoyol!

140
00:05:59,152 --> 00:06:01,054
(Solid defense)

141
00:06:01,054 --> 00:06:01,855
Hit it!

142
00:06:03,223 --> 00:06:05,425
Time for a straight shot.
They pass it, and...

143
00:06:06,993 --> 00:06:09,829
(Jin and Hyeon Jeong mixed
up the defensive call.)

144
00:06:10,029 --> 00:06:10,896
Hey!

145
00:06:12,565 --> 00:06:13,766
My mistake.

146
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:16,068
Jin, of course that was yours to set.

147
00:06:16,069 --> 00:06:17,537
Right, sorry.

148
00:06:19,005 --> 00:06:20,440
(Lost their chance to come back)

149
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,408
Sorry.

150
00:06:21,941 --> 00:06:23,009
Get ready.

151
00:06:23,009 --> 00:06:25,845
Da Bin, your dig was a control miss too.

152
00:06:25,845 --> 00:06:27,347
- Yes.
- That's not how you should've done it.

153
00:06:28,348 --> 00:06:29,782
A little bit more?

154
00:06:29,782 --> 00:06:31,250
Yes. The set keeps losing its flow.

155
00:06:31,250 --> 00:06:33,185
I'll go in faster. Just set it lower.

156
00:06:33,186 --> 00:06:34,921
Just let me know.

157
00:06:34,921 --> 00:06:36,790
(Who's next to serve?)

158
00:06:36,990 --> 00:06:37,824
A faster one?

159
00:06:38,358 --> 00:06:41,328
(Eun Ji made 20 ace serves
during the 2024-2025 season.)

160
00:06:42,662 --> 00:06:44,130
Left, guys.

161
00:06:45,098 --> 00:06:48,868
(Wonder Dogs prepped
against the left-hand server, Eun Ji.)

162
00:06:49,068 --> 00:06:49,802
Got it?

163
00:06:50,336 --> 00:06:51,537
Turn your body more. That's it.

164
00:06:51,638 --> 00:06:54,507
Just turn your body to the left. Got it?

165
00:06:54,874 --> 00:06:57,109
(We are ready.)

166
00:06:57,443 --> 00:07:01,314
(Feeling nervous)

167
00:07:03,883 --> 00:07:04,784
Serve.

168
00:07:07,387 --> 00:07:08,521
(Received)

169
00:07:08,921 --> 00:07:10,456
Yes. Nice catch.

170
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:11,657
Jin.

171
00:07:12,091 --> 00:07:12,992
Enkhsoyol.

172
00:07:13,259 --> 00:07:14,060
Hey!

173
00:07:14,594 --> 00:07:15,795
Hit it.

174
00:07:16,329 --> 00:07:17,764
Seon Ok spikes!

175
00:07:18,231 --> 00:07:19,165
(Solid blocking)

176
00:07:19,766 --> 00:07:21,067
Hit it!

177
00:07:21,668 --> 00:07:22,402
My!

178
00:07:22,635 --> 00:07:24,337
Hye In chases the ball. She can set it.

179
00:07:24,337 --> 00:07:25,304
Song Hee!
Hit it!

180
00:07:27,507 --> 00:07:29,943
A tip. Hyo Seo follows up and digs.

181
00:07:31,244 --> 00:07:32,078
Seon Ok.

182
00:07:32,812 --> 00:07:33,913
(It's blocked again!)

183
00:07:33,913 --> 00:07:35,214
It's blocked again.

184
00:07:36,783 --> 00:07:37,884
(Moving fast)

185
00:07:38,151 --> 00:07:39,219
Ho Bin attacks,

186
00:07:40,253 --> 00:07:41,287
but it's blocked.

187
00:07:41,754 --> 00:07:43,356
(Next attack is...)

188
00:07:43,990 --> 00:07:45,324
(Seon Ok's fourth try!)

189
00:07:45,324 --> 00:07:46,392
A jump up spike!

190
00:07:46,392 --> 00:07:49,195
(The block was finally broken through.)

191
00:07:49,195 --> 00:07:51,964
- Darn it.
- It's okay. It's only one point.

192
00:07:51,964 --> 00:07:53,766
(We still have chances.)

193
00:07:53,766 --> 00:07:54,967
Let's go right away!

194
00:07:55,335 --> 00:07:56,670
Be confident with your service!

195
00:07:56,936 --> 00:07:57,904
Yes, Coach.

196
00:07:58,104 --> 00:08:00,172
You swing too fast.

197
00:08:00,173 --> 00:08:01,641
Wait out a bit before you hit.

198
00:08:01,641 --> 00:08:02,475
Okay.

199
00:08:03,042 --> 00:08:04,210
The score is 2 to 4.

200
00:08:05,011 --> 00:08:07,280
Stay calm and wait for the timing.

201
00:08:11,517 --> 00:08:12,718
That's it.

202
00:08:13,386 --> 00:08:14,854
Jin jumps and sets it up.

203
00:08:14,854 --> 00:08:15,688
Enkhsoyol.

204
00:08:16,422 --> 00:08:18,391
(Eun Ji's diving dig)

205
00:08:18,391 --> 00:08:20,293
They've made the defense,
but can't attack.

206
00:08:20,293 --> 00:08:21,828
My ball!

207
00:08:22,095 --> 00:08:23,196
(Quick attack block)

208
00:08:23,196 --> 00:08:24,764
They blocked it right above.

209
00:08:26,032 --> 00:08:27,033
Our free ball!

210
00:08:32,438 --> 00:08:33,472
Hye In's dig.

211
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:36,075
Jin set it, and Enkhsoyol.

212
00:08:37,410 --> 00:08:38,578
(It's blocked again.)

213
00:08:39,245 --> 00:08:40,246
Hit it!

214
00:08:40,246 --> 00:08:41,848
(Seon Ok's attack again)

215
00:08:43,316 --> 00:08:45,818
It hits the blockers, and it's out.

216
00:08:45,818 --> 00:08:48,554
(A blocker touch out)

217
00:08:49,288 --> 00:08:51,657
(That's what I'm talking about.)

218
00:08:51,657 --> 00:08:52,558
Okay!

219
00:08:55,328 --> 00:08:59,765
(Block broken down once again
after a long rally)

220
00:08:59,765 --> 00:09:00,699
Sorry.

221
00:09:01,033 --> 00:09:03,235
The Wonder Dogs' attack is
too predictable.

222
00:09:03,536 --> 00:09:06,472
Their defense is on point,
but their offense is too predictable.

223
00:09:06,472 --> 00:09:09,408
Hye In is performing
amazing digs for defense.

224
00:09:09,559 --> 00:09:12,178
Their attacks are too predictable,

225
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,371
so the other team is ready for it
every time.

226
00:09:22,323 --> 00:09:26,594
(The Wonder Dogs' timeout)

227
00:09:26,805 --> 00:09:28,228
Why are you giving it to C when it's a B?

228
00:09:29,584 --> 00:09:32,444
Why are you setting B on receive
and then giving it to C?

229
00:09:34,168 --> 00:09:36,604
(When Hyeon Jeong...)

230
00:09:37,271 --> 00:09:38,739
(faked a jump in B,)

231
00:09:39,506 --> 00:09:42,008
(she tossed to Enkhsoyol,
who is right next to her in C.)

232
00:09:42,877 --> 00:09:46,214
(But two players are already blocking.)

233
00:09:46,341 --> 00:09:48,088
- Why did you do that?
- I shouldn't have.

234
00:09:48,089 --> 00:09:50,049
You can't play it like that. Come here.

235
00:09:50,427 --> 00:09:51,427
Get over here.

236
00:09:51,914 --> 00:09:54,055
Didn't I tell you
that they'd move to this side?

237
00:09:54,056 --> 00:09:57,925
- Yes, you did.
- You're drawing the blockers in.

238
00:09:57,986 --> 00:10:00,746
It's early in the second set,
and the Wonder Dogs are...

239
00:10:01,113 --> 00:10:04,972
relying on Enkhsoyol for offense.

240
00:10:04,973 --> 00:10:07,735
Seung Ju and Song Hee need
to contribute too.

241
00:10:09,331 --> 00:10:12,640
Seo Hyun, don't let Enkhsoyol fool you
with the feint.

242
00:10:12,641 --> 00:10:15,042
Enkhsoyol is not swinging
in a straight line.

243
00:10:15,110 --> 00:10:16,877
- You'd know it after the first set.
- Yes, Coach.

244
00:10:17,203 --> 00:10:18,656
Da Bin is doing well in defense.

245
00:10:19,003 --> 00:10:22,416
Don't try to get Enkhsoyol's ball.

246
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:25,908
- Let's go!
- Let's run harder!

247
00:10:26,153 --> 00:10:30,324
- We just need one point.
- Just one point!

248
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:32,093
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

249
00:10:37,631 --> 00:10:42,202
(Second set, Red Sparks 5 : Wonder Dogs 3)

250
00:10:42,636 --> 00:10:44,238
(It's not too late.)

251
00:10:44,239 --> 00:10:45,606
Target in between.

252
00:10:47,510 --> 00:10:48,942
- Serve!
- Serve by Enkhsoyol.

253
00:10:55,995 --> 00:10:57,351
Get it!

254
00:10:58,352 --> 00:10:59,987
(Jin's underhand toss)

255
00:10:59,988 --> 00:11:00,988
Hit it!

256
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:05,525
(Direct attack)

257
00:11:07,328 --> 00:11:09,730
(Jin's toss went over the net.)

258
00:11:14,783 --> 00:11:18,172
Song Hee, what happened on that dig?

259
00:11:18,173 --> 00:11:19,262
My mistake.

260
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:26,233
Seo Hyun.

261
00:11:26,347 --> 00:11:28,816
(You're getting even better.)

262
00:11:28,999 --> 00:11:30,017
I'm sorry.

263
00:11:30,999 --> 00:11:32,152
Sorry, Jin.

264
00:11:33,554 --> 00:11:35,156
(The rally continues.)

265
00:11:37,924 --> 00:11:39,694
- It slipped.
- The reception is shaky again.

266
00:11:40,897 --> 00:11:42,096
To Hyeon Jeong.

267
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:43,869
There you go.

268
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,769
Da Bin hits it.

269
00:11:48,802 --> 00:11:49,996
(Hye In dives for the dig.)

270
00:11:49,997 --> 00:11:51,305
- That's good.
- The ball is up in the air.

271
00:11:52,139 --> 00:11:54,475
(Jin jumps for it.)

272
00:11:55,655 --> 00:11:58,124
(It's out.)

273
00:11:59,113 --> 00:12:01,415
(The duo that led the attacks
in the first set)

274
00:12:01,648 --> 00:12:06,453
(The Jin and Song Hee duo)

275
00:12:08,674 --> 00:12:11,422
It seems the Wonder Dogs are...

276
00:12:11,755 --> 00:12:14,895
collapsing on their own right now.

277
00:12:16,976 --> 00:12:17,976
Jin.

278
00:12:19,342 --> 00:12:22,848
It was a tough call.

279
00:12:22,849 --> 00:12:25,305
We had no one left to sub in.

280
00:12:25,306 --> 00:12:26,740
(But the risks are too big
to sub a player.)

281
00:12:27,074 --> 00:12:29,810
(What's the rookie coach's decision?)

282
00:12:30,144 --> 00:12:32,087
(Na Yeon)

283
00:12:32,088 --> 00:12:33,247
Na Yeon!

284
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:37,639
Jin goes out, and Na Yeon comes in.

285
00:12:40,046 --> 00:12:41,722
Sol went out early in the game,

286
00:12:41,723 --> 00:12:46,227
and the match went well
because Jin held up so well.

287
00:12:46,228 --> 00:12:48,451
Now, it's up to Na Yeon to do the same.

288
00:12:51,165 --> 00:12:55,336
(Serve by Seon Ok)

289
00:12:56,463 --> 00:12:57,463
The score is 3 to 7.

290
00:12:58,305 --> 00:13:01,408
(Another short reception)

291
00:13:01,775 --> 00:13:02,709
- Mine.
- Hit it.

292
00:13:04,467 --> 00:13:07,147
Seung Ju with the straight shot.

293
00:13:07,554 --> 00:13:10,050
Let's build the momentum.

294
00:13:11,018 --> 00:13:12,720
(With Na Yeon's quick setup,)

295
00:13:12,721 --> 00:13:14,889
As soon as she's in, she changes
the flow of the game.

296
00:13:14,890 --> 00:13:16,557
(the ball goes perfectly
to Seung Ju on the far side.)

297
00:13:17,177 --> 00:13:19,052
Just side them out.

298
00:13:22,478 --> 00:13:24,064
The score is 4 to 8.
They're 4 points apart.

299
00:13:24,065 --> 00:13:27,501
(Second set, Red Sparks 8 : Wonder Dogs 4)

300
00:13:28,302 --> 00:13:30,070
(The rally continues.)

301
00:13:30,304 --> 00:13:31,304
Na Yeon sets it up.

302
00:13:33,379 --> 00:13:36,373
Seung Ju scores off the block.

303
00:13:36,730 --> 00:13:37,804
Nice!

304
00:13:37,979 --> 00:13:40,839
Seung Ju, keep playing like that.
That was good.

305
00:13:44,492 --> 00:13:45,645
- It's fine.
- Okay.

306
00:13:47,491 --> 00:13:49,957
Don't let their good plays get
in your head.

307
00:13:50,691 --> 00:13:52,693
(He's clearly bothered by it.)

308
00:13:53,530 --> 00:13:55,590
They're still only three points apart.

309
00:14:00,533 --> 00:14:01,635
Da Bin goes for it.

310
00:14:01,869 --> 00:14:03,437
(Da Bin hits it.)

311
00:14:04,056 --> 00:14:05,308
She dives to save the ball.

312
00:14:05,639 --> 00:14:07,407
(Hye In saves it again.)

313
00:14:07,434 --> 00:14:08,434
Pass it.

314
00:14:09,573 --> 00:14:10,714
Na Yeon sets it up,

315
00:14:12,194 --> 00:14:15,883
and Seung Ju scores again!

316
00:14:17,284 --> 00:14:20,320
(Captain Pyo is back.)

317
00:14:20,736 --> 00:14:22,856
Na Yeon came in,

318
00:14:23,102 --> 00:14:25,721
and since they're the same age
and joined the team in the same year,

319
00:14:25,727 --> 00:14:26,934
Seung Ju is getting her rhythm back.

320
00:14:26,935 --> 00:14:29,497
Hitters and setters all have...

321
00:14:29,681 --> 00:14:33,099
a style of play that fits
each player's own temperament.

322
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:36,870
Na Yeon is confident
in playing at the front.

323
00:14:36,919 --> 00:14:40,140
This brings out the speed,
and Seung Ju loves fastballs.

324
00:14:43,744 --> 00:14:45,980
(Only two points apart)

325
00:14:46,346 --> 00:14:50,217
(A perfect chance to chase)

326
00:14:50,617 --> 00:14:53,720
(It's time to make a winning move.)

327
00:14:54,783 --> 00:14:56,876
Song Hee's offense isn't working.

328
00:14:56,877 --> 00:15:00,360
Should we swap her with Tamira?

329
00:15:00,442 --> 00:15:02,442
Yes, we're lacking firepower.

330
00:15:02,636 --> 00:15:05,399
- We need to attack right now.
- You're right.

331
00:15:05,548 --> 00:15:07,681
Should we bring in Tamira now?

332
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:09,169
- Let's do it.
- Tamira!

333
00:15:10,021 --> 00:15:11,137
- Tamira.
- Yes?

334
00:15:12,266 --> 00:15:13,273
Tamira.

335
00:15:16,659 --> 00:15:17,711
You're subbing in for Song Hee.

336
00:15:17,712 --> 00:15:20,246
(The rookie coach plays her big card.)

337
00:15:20,559 --> 00:15:24,017
Coach Yeon Koung adds more firepower.

338
00:15:24,018 --> 00:15:25,218
Tamira is in.

339
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:27,554
Tamira, hold your position.

340
00:15:27,631 --> 00:15:29,823
You're in Zone Four. Set it to the center.

341
00:15:30,047 --> 00:15:31,160
Set it to the center.

342
00:15:31,693 --> 00:15:35,629
Hye Min, Da Bin, and Eun Ji.
Set the ball to the center,

343
00:15:35,750 --> 00:15:38,098
and when it floats straight up,
always block between your arms.

344
00:15:38,697 --> 00:15:41,702
And absolutely don't touch it. Got it?

345
00:15:41,969 --> 00:15:45,172
(Set it to the center.)

346
00:15:45,472 --> 00:15:47,641
(Instructing a serve to Zone Three)

347
00:15:48,242 --> 00:15:50,611
(The target zone)

348
00:15:51,711 --> 00:15:54,480
(Serve by Captain Pyo,
who is back in her groove)

349
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:00,747
- The reception is shaky.
- It's working.

350
00:16:01,054 --> 00:16:02,188
(But the ball...)

351
00:16:02,556 --> 00:16:04,358
(goes to Eun Ji.)

352
00:16:05,392 --> 00:16:06,627
(Wall Myoung Hwa is on the move.)

353
00:16:07,527 --> 00:16:08,695
(The ball is up high.)

354
00:16:08,928 --> 00:16:10,731
Nice!

355
00:16:14,534 --> 00:16:15,668
(The ball lands out.)

356
00:16:15,902 --> 00:16:17,216
(Myoung Hwa scores off the block.)

357
00:16:17,217 --> 00:16:18,605
Nice play!

358
00:16:18,989 --> 00:16:21,408
Myoung Hwa nailed it!

359
00:16:22,055 --> 00:16:23,376
The player of the day, Myoung Hwa!

360
00:16:23,910 --> 00:16:26,346
(The textbook example
of blocking with your arms closed)

361
00:16:27,247 --> 00:16:30,717
(That's how you block, Tamira.)

362
00:16:33,387 --> 00:16:36,357
(I got it!)

363
00:16:43,597 --> 00:16:48,168
(The Wonder Dogs are close behind them.)

364
00:16:48,635 --> 00:16:52,539
(They're just one point behind.)

365
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:54,350
Da Bin.

366
00:16:55,901 --> 00:16:58,011
Seung Ju receives it
and passes it to Na Yeon.

367
00:16:59,389 --> 00:17:00,453
Enkhsoyol spikes!

368
00:17:00,454 --> 00:17:02,096
There's a diving dig. And to Hyo Seo.

369
00:17:03,050 --> 00:17:06,387
(Tamira's solo block?)

370
00:17:06,653 --> 00:17:10,323
(Wall Myoung Hwa is on the move.)

371
00:17:11,658 --> 00:17:13,767
(A tying block by Myoung Hwa)

372
00:17:13,768 --> 00:17:15,666
Myoung Hwa!

373
00:17:16,963 --> 00:17:20,066
(Watching Professor Moon's block up close)

374
00:17:20,089 --> 00:17:22,269
Nice, Myoung Hwa!

375
00:17:25,081 --> 00:17:26,668
Here's the thing.

376
00:17:26,669 --> 00:17:28,742
In pro games,

377
00:17:28,743 --> 00:17:30,809
each team has its strengths.

378
00:17:30,810 --> 00:17:34,548
Once a team's strength starts showing,
it gains momentum.

379
00:17:34,594 --> 00:17:37,818
The Wonder Dogs play better
when their blocking works.

380
00:17:37,819 --> 00:17:39,220
(The Wonder Dogs' strength is blocking.)

381
00:17:39,486 --> 00:17:45,792
(Humming a theme song)

382
00:17:46,893 --> 00:17:52,132
(To seal the comeback,)

383
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:55,836
(I'm here.)

384
00:17:56,737 --> 00:17:59,974
(Serve by Myoung Hwa)

385
00:18:01,842 --> 00:18:03,477
(Starting with the service queen)

386
00:18:07,314 --> 00:18:09,750
(Hyeon Jeong pushes it over.)

387
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:15,222
(And here it comes.)

388
00:18:18,225 --> 00:18:22,596
(Enkhsoyol's block)

389
00:18:25,758 --> 00:18:29,350
They didn't finish it,
and the Wonder Dogs take the lead!

390
00:18:29,351 --> 00:18:33,206
(Successful reversal)

391
00:18:36,643 --> 00:18:38,044
Myoung Hwa, nice serve!

392
00:18:38,302 --> 00:18:39,679
Myoung Hwa, nice serve!

393
00:18:39,713 --> 00:18:43,083
(I'm unstoppable.)

394
00:18:49,144 --> 00:18:50,623
With Na Yeon in,

395
00:18:50,731 --> 00:18:53,560
Seung Ju's offense is revived.

396
00:18:53,790 --> 00:18:56,117
And Enkhsoyol has been playing solidly.

397
00:18:56,130 --> 00:18:58,765
- Their blocks are getting better too.
- That's right.

398
00:18:59,789 --> 00:19:02,969
Now they just need to widen the gap...

399
00:19:03,102 --> 00:19:05,102
- so they don't regret their play.
- Indeed.

400
00:19:05,849 --> 00:19:06,849
Zone Two.

401
00:19:07,908 --> 00:19:10,915
(The target zone)

402
00:19:12,082 --> 00:19:13,248
Moon Myoung Hwa.

403
00:19:13,248 --> 00:19:14,815
(The Serving Queen gets the ball again.)

404
00:19:15,448 --> 00:19:17,882
(Nervous)

405
00:19:22,282 --> 00:19:23,982
(A direct kill...)

406
00:19:23,982 --> 00:19:26,248
(once more?)

407
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:28,848
(It missed!)

408
00:19:29,048 --> 00:19:30,082
Tamira!

409
00:19:30,082 --> 00:19:31,548
(Enkhsoyol sets the ball up.)

410
00:19:33,482 --> 00:19:37,615
Spike by Tamira!

411
00:19:37,615 --> 00:19:38,915
- Yes!
- Let's go!

412
00:19:39,415 --> 00:19:41,382
(You did it.)

413
00:19:41,382 --> 00:19:44,048
(Go Tamira!)

414
00:19:47,682 --> 00:19:49,182
Enkhsoyol and Tamira.

415
00:19:49,182 --> 00:19:52,115
They're the top hitters
in the university league.

416
00:19:53,715 --> 00:19:58,348
(Tamira and Enkhsoyol's
perfect combo play)

417
00:19:58,915 --> 00:20:01,415
They're two points ahead.
Myoung Hwa serves again.

418
00:20:04,982 --> 00:20:06,148
Their reception is shaky!

419
00:20:08,015 --> 00:20:09,015
(Glaring)

420
00:20:09,015 --> 00:20:10,048
The ball is over.

421
00:20:10,182 --> 00:20:11,182
Slowly!

422
00:20:11,182 --> 00:20:12,515
- Lee Na Yeon.
- Hit it!

423
00:20:12,515 --> 00:20:13,915
- Spike!
- Go.

424
00:20:14,215 --> 00:20:15,248
Right!

425
00:20:15,482 --> 00:20:17,248
- Cover!
- Cover her!

426
00:20:17,682 --> 00:20:20,182
(Shin Eun Ji's straight shot)

427
00:20:23,082 --> 00:20:24,115
That was a nice hit.

428
00:20:24,115 --> 00:20:26,515
She went for a straight shot
when the inside was blocked.

429
00:20:27,382 --> 00:20:29,515
(Satisfied)

430
00:20:33,648 --> 00:20:35,348
(Coach Kim is suddenly lost in thought?)

431
00:20:35,515 --> 00:20:37,448
One more point. Where were you going?

432
00:20:39,248 --> 00:20:41,215
(Nodding)

433
00:20:46,715 --> 00:20:48,215
Let's do it.

434
00:20:49,815 --> 00:20:50,915
Go.

435
00:20:50,915 --> 00:20:52,315
It touched it.

436
00:20:52,315 --> 00:20:53,882
- Was it the setter's back-row hit?
- Yes.

437
00:20:54,848 --> 00:20:56,648
She's requesting a video review.

438
00:20:57,382 --> 00:20:59,482
I think it went over.

439
00:21:00,282 --> 00:21:04,182
She asked for a video review
regarding a back-row hit fault.

440
00:21:04,715 --> 00:21:07,882
- That means the setter was at the back.
- Yes. When the Red Sparks' setter...

441
00:21:07,882 --> 00:21:10,048
was at the back but touched the ball,

442
00:21:10,048 --> 00:21:12,215
- It's an attack.
- it's considered an attack.

443
00:21:12,215 --> 00:21:13,748
(It's a fault when she touches
the ball over the net.)

444
00:21:15,048 --> 00:21:16,648
Hyeon Jeong was about to attack.

445
00:21:17,548 --> 00:21:21,182
The ball goes over the net...

446
00:21:22,682 --> 00:21:25,982
(She touched the ball
when it went over the net.)

447
00:21:26,582 --> 00:21:29,182
It's ruled as a back-row hitter's fault.

448
00:21:29,682 --> 00:21:31,548
- They saw it as an attack.
- You're right.

449
00:21:32,982 --> 00:21:35,115
(Dumbfounded)

450
00:21:35,982 --> 00:21:38,048
How did Coach see that?

451
00:21:39,115 --> 00:21:41,348
(I'm keeping this momentum.)

452
00:21:41,548 --> 00:21:42,548
It's 13 to 11.

453
00:21:42,548 --> 00:21:44,082
(Second set, Red Sparks 11
: Wonder Dogs 13)

454
00:21:44,082 --> 00:21:45,915
Send it right away!

455
00:21:46,348 --> 00:21:47,915
(We must widen the gap
while we have the momentum.)

456
00:21:47,915 --> 00:21:49,215
Catch!

457
00:21:49,815 --> 00:21:51,515
The serve isn't strong. It's floating.

458
00:21:52,215 --> 00:21:53,582
An Ye Rim serves.

459
00:21:56,382 --> 00:21:58,082
- Kim Hyeon Jeong.
- Enkhsoyol!

460
00:21:58,082 --> 00:21:59,082
(The ball is tossed to Enkhsoyol.)

461
00:21:59,582 --> 00:22:00,615
Enkhsoyol.

462
00:22:01,282 --> 00:22:02,615
The Red Sparks save it.

463
00:22:03,382 --> 00:22:04,548
Gwak Seon Ok's spike.

464
00:22:05,615 --> 00:22:07,348
(It's their chance to attack again.)

465
00:22:07,882 --> 00:22:08,982
- Right!
- Seo Hyun!

466
00:22:09,715 --> 00:22:11,582
(Right?)

467
00:22:11,582 --> 00:22:12,582
They're going left again.

468
00:22:13,682 --> 00:22:15,915
(Just as she expected!)

469
00:22:17,948 --> 00:22:21,048
(Always block between your hands.)

470
00:22:23,215 --> 00:22:24,948
(Tamira follows it smoothly.)

471
00:22:26,348 --> 00:22:29,615
- The ball goes in.
- Tamira's block!

472
00:22:30,548 --> 00:22:32,915
(Professor Moon is satisfied.)

473
00:22:34,248 --> 00:22:36,482
(And so is the rookie coach.)

474
00:22:36,982 --> 00:22:38,715
(He is not satisfied.)

475
00:22:39,815 --> 00:22:40,915
Pyo Seung Ju's reception.

476
00:22:41,948 --> 00:22:43,382
(Enkhsoyol's spike)

477
00:22:43,382 --> 00:22:45,782
A great shot by Enkhsoyol!

478
00:22:47,482 --> 00:22:48,482
Nice catch.

479
00:22:50,882 --> 00:22:51,982
(A successful reception)

480
00:22:52,448 --> 00:22:54,648
(This time...)

481
00:22:54,648 --> 00:22:55,848
Kim Hyeon Jeong's slide attack!

482
00:22:59,282 --> 00:23:00,282
She did it!

483
00:23:01,948 --> 00:23:03,748
(Second set, Red Sparks 14
: Wonder Dogs 16)

484
00:23:03,748 --> 00:23:04,815
Mine.

485
00:23:04,948 --> 00:23:05,982
Enkhsoyol receives the ball.

486
00:23:06,948 --> 00:23:07,948
(Pyo Seung Ju spikes.)
Pyo Seung Ju.

487
00:23:09,282 --> 00:23:10,482
Their reception turns unstable.

488
00:23:11,015 --> 00:23:13,582
They sent the ball over.
Koo Hye In calmly receives it.

489
00:23:13,982 --> 00:23:16,682
Lee Na Yeon tosses,
and Pyo Seung Ju tips once more!

490
00:23:17,482 --> 00:23:19,982
It's shaky again. An Ye Rim!

491
00:23:21,348 --> 00:23:24,482
The ball is blocked.

492
00:23:27,715 --> 00:23:29,848
Nice. Way to go.

493
00:23:29,848 --> 00:23:31,982
Nice!

494
00:23:31,982 --> 00:23:33,982
(The Wonder Dogs are on a roll now.)

495
00:23:35,715 --> 00:23:36,982
They're now four points apart.

496
00:23:36,982 --> 00:23:38,048
(Red Sparks 16 : Wonder Dogs 20)

497
00:23:41,915 --> 00:23:44,015
Second request for a timeout.

498
00:23:44,015 --> 00:23:45,748
(The Red Sparks call a timeout.)

499
00:23:49,348 --> 00:23:51,515
Get out if you want to play it safe.

500
00:23:51,782 --> 00:23:52,948
- No.
- No, Coach!

501
00:23:54,882 --> 00:23:57,948
Do you seriously not know what to do?

502
00:23:59,915 --> 00:24:03,348
Play properly at least
before losing a point.

503
00:24:03,348 --> 00:24:04,515
- Yes!
- Yes!

504
00:24:07,048 --> 00:24:08,315
This isn't a joke.

505
00:24:08,315 --> 00:24:09,315
- Yes!
- Yes!

506
00:24:09,682 --> 00:24:10,948
Let's go!

507
00:24:10,948 --> 00:24:12,582
Red Sparks!

508
00:24:14,582 --> 00:24:15,648
Hye Min.

509
00:24:16,748 --> 00:24:19,215
- Serve slowly, Hye Min.
- Yes, Coach.

510
00:24:20,215 --> 00:24:22,548
He decides to put Park Hye Min in.

511
00:24:22,548 --> 00:24:23,882
Nice serve!

512
00:24:25,182 --> 00:24:26,382
(Glancing)

513
00:24:27,848 --> 00:24:30,882
The serve is not strong.
It's floating a lot and slowly!

514
00:24:31,715 --> 00:24:33,215
(They buzz as Park Hye Min enters.)

515
00:24:33,215 --> 00:24:34,615
It's a short one!

516
00:24:36,082 --> 00:24:37,115
(Tapping)

517
00:24:43,315 --> 00:24:45,615
Hye In receives it,
and Na Yeon jumps to toss.

518
00:24:45,615 --> 00:24:46,782
(The ball is set up...)

519
00:24:47,048 --> 00:24:48,982
(and Enkhsoyol is ready to attack.)

520
00:24:49,115 --> 00:24:50,115
Nice toss.

521
00:24:50,115 --> 00:24:51,182
Hit it!

522
00:24:51,582 --> 00:24:52,615
Enkhsoyol.

523
00:24:53,848 --> 00:24:55,482
But the Red Sparks defend.

524
00:24:55,615 --> 00:24:56,648
Seon Ok!

525
00:24:58,315 --> 00:24:59,815
Hit it!

526
00:24:59,848 --> 00:25:03,315
Seon Ok spikes! It's a bullseye.

527
00:25:03,315 --> 00:25:05,215
(A spike to bring back the momentum)

528
00:25:07,182 --> 00:25:09,315
For the Red Sparks,

529
00:25:09,315 --> 00:25:13,348
they attack from various points to score.

530
00:25:13,348 --> 00:25:14,319
(A straight shot to an open spot)

531
00:25:15,248 --> 00:25:16,548
Great job.

532
00:25:16,548 --> 00:25:18,048
Nice hit!

533
00:25:19,515 --> 00:25:23,048
Myoung Hwa is out, and Su Bin is in.

534
00:25:23,315 --> 00:25:25,948
Choi Su Bin is not a libero today.

535
00:25:25,948 --> 00:25:27,115
Right.

536
00:25:27,115 --> 00:25:29,815
- She's what we call a pinch server.
- That's right.

537
00:25:32,848 --> 00:25:33,915
Mine.

538
00:25:36,048 --> 00:25:37,082
(A quick setup for attack)

539
00:25:37,082 --> 00:25:39,315
Hit it!

540
00:25:39,315 --> 00:25:41,282
Spike. They defended it.

541
00:25:41,282 --> 00:25:42,382
We have to send it over.

542
00:25:42,382 --> 00:25:43,515
That's a double touch.

543
00:25:44,582 --> 00:25:45,615
(The Red Sparks' free ball)

544
00:25:45,615 --> 00:25:46,648
Chae Na's back toss.

545
00:25:48,115 --> 00:25:50,382
(It's a tip this time.)

546
00:25:51,448 --> 00:25:52,448
Tip!

547
00:25:55,315 --> 00:25:57,315
- Tamira saved the ball!
- That's it!

548
00:25:58,182 --> 00:26:00,248
She did it.

549
00:26:00,248 --> 00:26:01,248
Set it up!

550
00:26:01,482 --> 00:26:02,482
Hit it!

551
00:26:03,548 --> 00:26:05,682
(Enkhsoyol spikes.)

552
00:26:05,682 --> 00:26:06,715
Enkhsoyol!

553
00:26:07,015 --> 00:26:08,648
(A line out)

554
00:26:08,782 --> 00:26:09,848
Nice!

555
00:26:14,782 --> 00:26:18,115
(Second set, Red Sparks 18
: Wonder Dogs 22)

556
00:26:18,115 --> 00:26:22,582
When they miss the opportunity
to attack for a point,

557
00:26:22,582 --> 00:26:25,748
- it won't be good later.
- It can become an obstacle.

558
00:26:27,382 --> 00:26:29,982
(The rookie coach is anxious.)

559
00:26:30,382 --> 00:26:32,815
(The next one to serve is...)

560
00:26:35,082 --> 00:26:36,648
(Tamira.)

561
00:26:36,648 --> 00:26:38,348
In between, Tamira.

562
00:26:41,548 --> 00:26:42,715
In 1, 2, 3.

563
00:26:42,715 --> 00:26:44,315
Nice serve!

564
00:26:49,048 --> 00:26:50,148
A sharp serve!

565
00:26:52,148 --> 00:26:53,515
She digs to receive it.

566
00:26:54,682 --> 00:26:55,782
The ball is blocked.

567
00:26:56,215 --> 00:26:57,215
Hit it!

568
00:26:57,215 --> 00:26:58,415
Gwak Seon Ok's standing jump.

569
00:26:59,282 --> 00:27:00,782
Hye In saves the ball.

570
00:27:00,782 --> 00:27:01,782
That's it!

571
00:27:03,248 --> 00:27:05,915
The ball heads to Enkhsoyol,
and she spikes!

572
00:27:07,115 --> 00:27:08,748
It hits the net, and they defend it.

573
00:27:09,248 --> 00:27:10,382
It's a tip. Get inside!

574
00:27:12,582 --> 00:27:13,615
Eun Ji's tip.

575
00:27:13,615 --> 00:27:14,648
To Hye In.

576
00:27:14,648 --> 00:27:15,715
Pipe.

577
00:27:16,648 --> 00:27:18,648
- Hit it!
- Pyo Seung Ju's back attack!

578
00:27:19,882 --> 00:27:20,915
Hit it!

579
00:27:20,915 --> 00:27:23,148
Out!

580
00:27:23,982 --> 00:27:26,115
(Is it in?)

581
00:27:26,115 --> 00:27:27,248
(Or out?)

582
00:27:28,682 --> 00:27:30,348
- It's out!
- Out!

583
00:27:30,348 --> 00:27:32,415
- Okay!
- Nice!

584
00:27:32,415 --> 00:27:35,448
(They're gradually losing momentum.)

585
00:27:37,515 --> 00:27:38,548
- Again!
- Let's do it again!

586
00:27:38,548 --> 00:27:40,248
They narrowed the gap to three points.

587
00:27:40,782 --> 00:27:45,582
The Wonder Dogs can't seem
to widen the gap.

588
00:27:45,582 --> 00:27:47,582
(They must do something to widen the gap.)

589
00:27:47,582 --> 00:27:48,682
Again.

590
00:27:49,515 --> 00:27:50,615
It's a drop!

591
00:27:50,615 --> 00:27:52,082
(The right area is empty?)

592
00:27:53,348 --> 00:27:54,448
Na Yeon.

593
00:27:54,448 --> 00:27:56,548
(Aim for the right area.)

594
00:27:56,548 --> 00:27:58,048
(Understood.)

595
00:27:59,882 --> 00:28:00,915
- Go quickly.
- Okay.

596
00:28:04,082 --> 00:28:05,082
Serve.

597
00:28:05,082 --> 00:28:06,148
(Eun Ji serves.)

598
00:28:07,782 --> 00:28:08,815
Na Yeon!

599
00:28:10,482 --> 00:28:11,948
(It's still empty!)

600
00:28:13,215 --> 00:28:14,948
(Oops!)

601
00:28:16,982 --> 00:28:17,982
Okay!

602
00:28:17,982 --> 00:28:19,348
Good job.

603
00:28:20,015 --> 00:28:22,548
She hits and scores with a blockout!

604
00:28:22,548 --> 00:28:24,648
Sorry. I should have seen it.

605
00:28:24,648 --> 00:28:25,748
What are you doing?

606
00:28:29,355 --> 00:28:31,115
(Let's get this going!)

607
00:28:31,115 --> 00:28:32,748
Nice one, Hyeon Jeong!

608
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:38,648
(The serve continues.)

609
00:28:38,648 --> 00:28:39,882
Enkhsoyol serves.

610
00:28:39,882 --> 00:28:41,282
(Strong Enkhsoyol serves.)

611
00:28:41,682 --> 00:28:44,315
In between, Enkhsoyol.

612
00:28:44,315 --> 00:28:45,615
Hit it softly. Go in between.

613
00:28:45,948 --> 00:28:47,148
Take it easy!

614
00:28:47,148 --> 00:28:49,515
In 2, 3. Nice serve!

615
00:28:49,515 --> 00:28:50,682
Get ready to set.

616
00:28:51,482 --> 00:28:52,848
Near the net!

617
00:28:52,848 --> 00:28:55,082
- She just needs to avoid errors.
- Exactly.

618
00:28:55,282 --> 00:28:56,282
Serve.

619
00:29:02,915 --> 00:29:05,115
(There's the pattern again.)

620
00:29:05,115 --> 00:29:06,115
I'm sorry.

621
00:29:08,280 --> 00:29:10,079
I told you to go in between.
Where were you aiming?

622
00:29:12,106 --> 00:29:15,202
I told you to go
for their in-between, okay?

623
00:29:16,742 --> 00:29:19,191
Red Sparks, Seon Ok's serve.

624
00:29:23,154 --> 00:29:25,646
The reception is too short.
The ball goes to Seung Ju.

625
00:29:25,733 --> 00:29:26,940
She tips the highball.

626
00:29:27,693 --> 00:29:29,307
She manages to set it.

627
00:29:29,673 --> 00:29:30,779
To the corner!

628
00:29:31,036 --> 00:29:31,737
(Moving)

629
00:29:32,805 --> 00:29:34,133
Eun Ji.

630
00:29:34,134 --> 00:29:36,475
- That's it!
- That's it! Tamira is amazing.

631
00:29:37,005 --> 00:29:38,132
The defense works. Na Yeon.

632
00:29:38,691 --> 00:29:39,691
Na Yeon, it's too short.

633
00:29:40,318 --> 00:29:44,457
Seung Ju! Seon Ok's dig.
Hyo Seo sets it to Eun Ji.

634
00:29:47,953 --> 00:29:49,354
(Is she breaking through?)

635
00:29:51,556 --> 00:29:53,425
- She saves it!
- That's it!

636
00:29:54,226 --> 00:29:55,327
She's ready!

637
00:29:58,731 --> 00:30:00,766
(Seung Ju's spike)

638
00:30:01,467 --> 00:30:03,402
(Did Captain Pyo just score a point?)

639
00:30:06,617 --> 00:30:08,464
It's a touch out!

640
00:30:09,908 --> 00:30:13,412
(Score!)

641
00:30:18,851 --> 00:30:21,253
(Thanks to Tamira's defense)

642
00:30:21,372 --> 00:30:24,756
It's 24 to 20.
It's Wonder Dogs' set point now.

643
00:30:25,658 --> 00:30:28,158
Let's get one more point!

644
00:30:28,159 --> 00:30:31,232
- Okay.
- Okay, we can do it!

645
00:30:31,233 --> 00:30:33,565
(One point will finish this rally!)

646
00:30:39,794 --> 00:30:41,674
Hyo Seo's stable reception.

647
00:30:41,675 --> 00:30:43,509
(Nice reception)

648
00:30:44,576 --> 00:30:47,412
(She charges toward the net immediately.)

649
00:30:47,746 --> 00:30:49,047
(Here they come!)

650
00:30:49,248 --> 00:30:51,450
(We need to block this!)

651
00:30:51,965 --> 00:30:53,738
She gets it up! Spike!

652
00:30:57,322 --> 00:31:00,458
(Did they fail to win the set here?)

653
00:31:01,980 --> 00:31:05,517
(She touched the net!)

654
00:31:06,665 --> 00:31:07,665
She touched it.

655
00:31:07,894 --> 00:31:09,414
- Okay, good job.
- Nice!

656
00:31:09,615 --> 00:31:12,554
She touched the net!
A net-touch violation.

657
00:31:12,555 --> 00:31:14,660
That's it!

658
00:31:16,094 --> 00:31:18,163
(We win the second set!)

659
00:31:19,764 --> 00:31:20,999
(He's not smiling anymore.)

660
00:31:21,439 --> 00:31:25,103
Wonder Dogs win the set 25 to 20.

661
00:31:26,171 --> 00:31:28,199
(Timeout before the third set)

662
00:31:28,232 --> 00:31:29,708
- Make a stronger serve.
- Okay.

663
00:31:29,751 --> 00:31:32,425
Na Yeon, focus on your aim when you serve,
just like I instructed you.

664
00:31:32,426 --> 00:31:36,081
Aim exactly where I tell you to.
We need to focus a little more on serving.

665
00:31:36,348 --> 00:31:38,395
- Just concentrate harder.
- Okay.

666
00:31:43,853 --> 00:31:46,825
When you served,

667
00:31:47,013 --> 00:31:49,536
I told you to make it short,
not the usual serve,

668
00:31:49,555 --> 00:31:51,896
but none of you listened
and made it short.

669
00:31:52,731 --> 00:31:54,399
That means you're not focusing
on the game.

670
00:31:56,248 --> 00:31:57,248
None of you.

671
00:31:57,781 --> 00:32:00,638
How easy does the game become
when you serve properly?

672
00:32:00,727 --> 00:32:03,094
- Okay!
- Let's go!

673
00:32:03,095 --> 00:32:04,810
(Both teams will focus harder on serving.)

674
00:32:04,873 --> 00:32:07,020
- In 1, 2, 3!
- Yes!

675
00:32:07,021 --> 00:32:08,213
The set score is 1 to 1.

676
00:32:09,407 --> 00:32:11,159
The match is back to square one.

677
00:32:12,392 --> 00:32:15,845
The third set, important
for both teams, begins.

678
00:32:16,922 --> 00:32:18,323
(Peeking)

679
00:32:18,857 --> 00:32:20,959
(She signals to aim at zone three.)

680
00:32:25,963 --> 00:32:27,232
The third set begins.

681
00:32:27,852 --> 00:32:28,852
(Groaning)

682
00:32:29,701 --> 00:32:31,770
(Her serve completely disrupted
the opponents.)

683
00:32:32,262 --> 00:32:33,411
Let's go, Tamira!

684
00:32:33,554 --> 00:32:35,334
(Target locked on)

685
00:32:37,175 --> 00:32:40,578
(Direct kill)

686
00:32:41,300 --> 00:32:42,547
No way.

687
00:32:47,652 --> 00:32:49,754
(Big smile)

688
00:32:50,989 --> 00:32:53,225
- Yes!
- Nice!

689
00:32:53,858 --> 00:32:58,029
(It's a good start.)

690
00:32:58,897 --> 00:33:01,933
(Na Yeon's serves again)

691
00:33:03,389 --> 00:33:04,389
The same spot!

692
00:33:06,882 --> 00:33:07,882
The score is 1 to 0.

693
00:33:09,808 --> 00:33:11,276
- Oh, no.
- Hey.

694
00:33:16,948 --> 00:33:19,517
(Myoung Hwa got fooled.)

695
00:33:22,011 --> 00:33:23,288
Da Bin spikes.

696
00:33:26,224 --> 00:33:26,691
Cover!

697
00:33:27,175 --> 00:33:28,626
Follow it!

698
00:33:29,575 --> 00:33:31,329
The ball hits Enkhsoyol's left arm!

699
00:33:32,949 --> 00:33:34,232
Hye In saves it!

700
00:33:35,266 --> 00:33:37,268
(She sets it right over.)

701
00:33:37,535 --> 00:33:40,605
(What's happening?)

702
00:33:40,719 --> 00:33:43,485
The ball flew outside the antenna.

703
00:33:45,131 --> 00:33:47,131
Still, it was amazing defense.

704
00:33:47,644 --> 00:33:49,748
Myoung Hwa, why did you move early?

705
00:33:51,316 --> 00:33:53,184
(Myoung Hwa moved
before the setter set it.)

706
00:33:53,185 --> 00:33:55,887
She got fooled by the setter.

707
00:33:57,288 --> 00:34:00,191
(By moving too early,
they failed to form a double block.)

708
00:34:01,468 --> 00:34:04,055
Just wait.

709
00:34:05,734 --> 00:34:07,574
The score is 1 to 1. Ye Rim.

710
00:34:08,677 --> 00:34:10,769
Go!

711
00:34:10,830 --> 00:34:12,933
Back toss. Spike by Tamira!

712
00:34:13,538 --> 00:34:15,093
(Seung Ju's dig)

713
00:34:15,094 --> 00:34:16,341
Seung Ju digs it!

714
00:34:18,459 --> 00:34:19,711
Here goes Tamira again.

715
00:34:24,969 --> 00:34:26,818
Eun Ji!

716
00:34:27,658 --> 00:34:29,950
No!

717
00:34:30,121 --> 00:34:32,190
(It's out.)

718
00:34:32,564 --> 00:34:34,810
- Good!
- It's in!

719
00:34:34,811 --> 00:34:36,395
Is it out after touching her?

720
00:34:36,809 --> 00:34:38,330
The referee calls it out.

721
00:34:40,861 --> 00:34:42,567
It didn't touch Seung Ju's hands.

722
00:34:44,488 --> 00:34:46,371
It went straight out.

723
00:34:46,840 --> 00:34:48,473
I didn't touch it.

724
00:34:48,727 --> 00:34:50,275
It's my mistake. Sorry.

725
00:34:50,586 --> 00:34:55,769
Eun Ji's attacks in the first
and second sets are clearly different.

726
00:34:55,770 --> 00:34:58,884
That's right. Only one attack worked
out of her 13 attempts in the second set.

727
00:34:58,982 --> 00:35:01,720
I'm sure Eun Ji will try even harder...

728
00:35:01,841 --> 00:35:03,922
to raise her attack efficiency
in this third set.

729
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:08,059
Come on, they're not even trying to score.

730
00:35:08,133 --> 00:35:10,953
When they block, you need
to spike properly, not half-heartedly.

731
00:35:11,229 --> 00:35:14,566
(He instructed her
to break through the block.)

732
00:35:14,879 --> 00:35:17,335
Enkhsoyol, don't let it be touch out.

733
00:35:17,336 --> 00:35:21,473
(You know what I mean, right?)

734
00:35:29,756 --> 00:35:30,916
Do it!

735
00:35:31,316 --> 00:35:34,452
(Will she break through?)

736
00:35:34,686 --> 00:35:37,856
(Or will they block her again?)

737
00:35:40,121 --> 00:35:41,626
The opponent's spike.

738
00:35:42,394 --> 00:35:43,695
It's a touch out.

739
00:35:44,529 --> 00:35:46,331
(That's it.)

740
00:35:46,447 --> 00:35:47,733
Oh, my gosh.

741
00:35:52,112 --> 00:35:54,112
It was too fast. Watch the timing.

742
00:35:55,140 --> 00:35:57,676
(Third Set, Red Sparks 3 : Wonder Dogs 4)

743
00:36:01,335 --> 00:36:02,335
Enkhsoyol's set.

744
00:36:05,617 --> 00:36:07,119
(Enkhsoyol's tip)

745
00:36:07,452 --> 00:36:08,753
(Confused)

746
00:36:11,122 --> 00:36:13,891
(Their countermove is also a tip.)

747
00:36:17,734 --> 00:36:19,898
What? How did she save that?

748
00:36:21,161 --> 00:36:24,569
- Amazing defense by Hye In!
- Nice defense.

749
00:36:35,035 --> 00:36:37,595
Spike! It's a touch out.

750
00:36:37,596 --> 00:36:39,918
(It's another blocker touch out.)

751
00:36:40,740 --> 00:36:42,247
I told you not to pull.

752
00:36:42,547 --> 00:36:44,155
If you hadn't pulled,
it would've gone out.

753
00:36:45,156 --> 00:36:48,693
(The Wonder Dogs' blocks...)

754
00:36:49,694 --> 00:36:53,598
(aren't working anymore.)

755
00:36:54,532 --> 00:36:57,568
(It's time to change the offense pattern.)

756
00:36:57,595 --> 00:36:59,104
Enkhsoyol, the ball wasn't good.

757
00:36:59,105 --> 00:37:01,903
- Just aim at a spot and go straight.
- Okay.

758
00:37:01,904 --> 00:37:04,009
- Get to your position!
- Aim at the spot.

759
00:37:05,210 --> 00:37:07,212
(During Wonder Dogs' possession,)

760
00:37:07,545 --> 00:37:10,548
(their corner back has been wide open.)

761
00:37:10,615 --> 00:37:13,135
What did I say about their defense?
They always move forward to the net.

762
00:37:13,136 --> 00:37:16,054
Then how do we attack?
You make it long to the back.

763
00:37:18,013 --> 00:37:19,190
It's 5 to 5, a tie.

764
00:37:22,942 --> 00:37:23,942
Enkhsoyol.

765
00:37:23,943 --> 00:37:24,963
Get it up!

766
00:37:31,536 --> 00:37:33,905
(Aim for the back!)

767
00:37:36,854 --> 00:37:39,911
Enkhsoyol's tip!

768
00:37:40,378 --> 00:37:43,114
(A clean, straight shot!)

769
00:37:46,679 --> 00:37:50,355
What are they doing playing
like volleyball newbies?

770
00:37:50,938 --> 00:37:54,691
See? All you need to do is
aim deep and go straight.

771
00:37:55,660 --> 00:37:57,777
(The match continues.)

772
00:37:57,777 --> 00:37:58,377
Hit it!

773
00:37:58,510 --> 00:37:59,444
Hit it!

774
00:38:00,899 --> 00:38:02,941
Seon Ok hits it down!

775
00:38:03,190 --> 00:38:04,124
Hyeon Jeong.

776
00:38:04,124 --> 00:38:06,126
(Third set, Red Sparks 6 : Wonder Dogs 6)

777
00:38:06,126 --> 00:38:07,561
- Hit it!
- Go!

778
00:38:08,462 --> 00:38:09,596
Seung Ju's faint tip!

779
00:38:10,130 --> 00:38:11,965
Score. It worked.

780
00:38:12,599 --> 00:38:15,168
(Second set, Red Sparks 6 : Wonder Dogs 7)

781
00:38:16,169 --> 00:38:17,137
Go!

782
00:38:17,571 --> 00:38:19,172
Spikes!

783
00:38:19,172 --> 00:38:21,608
(Another head-on battle at the net)

784
00:38:21,608 --> 00:38:24,811
The opponent is
breaking our blocking efficiently.

785
00:38:25,445 --> 00:38:26,913
The point-by-point battle is
getting intense.

786
00:38:26,913 --> 00:38:28,348
The score is tied at 7 to 7.

787
00:38:30,284 --> 00:38:31,619
Na Yeon!

788
00:38:33,186 --> 00:38:35,155
Na Yeon, this one.

789
00:38:35,155 --> 00:38:36,056
Okay.

790
00:38:37,291 --> 00:38:38,291
(Newbie coach's sign)

791
00:38:38,291 --> 00:38:40,026
Let's go right away.

792
00:38:40,027 --> 00:38:41,695
Let's go, guys.

793
00:38:43,697 --> 00:38:44,498
Here.

794
00:38:46,266 --> 00:38:47,167
Got it.

795
00:38:47,167 --> 00:38:48,735
(Na Yeon and Myoung Hwa exchange signs.)

796
00:38:49,770 --> 00:38:51,038
Stay focused!

797
00:38:51,405 --> 00:38:52,873
(Seon Ok's serving in an intense flow.)

798
00:38:52,873 --> 00:38:53,974
It's a tie.

799
00:38:53,974 --> 00:38:55,409
(Seon Ok's serving in an intense flow)

800
00:38:57,878 --> 00:38:58,712
Up high.

801
00:39:00,247 --> 00:39:02,416
Quick attack by Myoung Hwa!

802
00:39:02,416 --> 00:39:03,984
Okay!

803
00:39:04,518 --> 00:39:05,886
- Nice, Myoung Hwa.
- Nice!

804
00:39:05,886 --> 00:39:06,753
Nice one, Myoung Hwa.

805
00:39:06,753 --> 00:39:08,622
- Nice. Okay.
- Nice job!

806
00:39:09,957 --> 00:39:11,191
Sorry.

807
00:39:13,460 --> 00:39:16,396
- Great. We even scored a quick attack.
- Right.

808
00:39:16,530 --> 00:39:18,832
Our two-player attacks are
too predictable.

809
00:39:18,832 --> 00:39:21,001
We're only hitting the left.

810
00:39:21,001 --> 00:39:23,103
We have to roll in back attacks
or the middle too.

811
00:39:23,103 --> 00:39:24,304
Even if we don't make it.

812
00:39:24,671 --> 00:39:25,939
For the opponent.

813
00:39:26,974 --> 00:39:30,578
(Left attacks worked in the beginning.)

814
00:39:30,711 --> 00:39:31,712
- Enkhsoyol!
- Hit it!

815
00:39:32,345 --> 00:39:35,915
(But as the game went on,
they started to block their left attacks.)

816
00:39:36,416 --> 00:39:39,886
Do our setters not like Myoung Hwa?
Let her have the ball once in a while.

817
00:39:40,153 --> 00:39:41,843
(Use Myoung Hwa?)

818
00:39:41,844 --> 00:39:44,175
We need to use more of the middle.

819
00:39:44,175 --> 00:39:47,227
(Center attack using the middle blocker)

820
00:39:48,028 --> 00:39:53,467
(Verifying attack routes so that
the opponent's blocking could scatter)

821
00:39:54,501 --> 00:39:56,903
(The masterstroke of the third set is...)

822
00:39:56,903 --> 00:39:59,773
(the middle attack.)

823
00:40:02,743 --> 00:40:06,480
Ye Rim, watch out for the quick attack.
And stay on the right side.

824
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:07,314
Okay.

825
00:40:08,348 --> 00:40:09,983
- One, two!
- Mine!

826
00:40:10,283 --> 00:40:11,484
Hye In set it up.

827
00:40:11,485 --> 00:40:13,286
(Center or left?)

828
00:40:13,286 --> 00:40:15,088
Show them what you've got.
This is your chance.

829
00:40:15,088 --> 00:40:16,456
Attack, Myoung Hwa.

830
00:40:19,726 --> 00:40:21,628
(Here comes the middle quick attack.)

831
00:40:22,663 --> 00:40:25,065
(It's way too fast and strong!)

832
00:40:26,433 --> 00:40:28,635
(Two quick attacks in the blink of an eye)

833
00:40:28,835 --> 00:40:29,736
Nice!

834
00:40:29,736 --> 00:40:31,238
(Laughing)

835
00:40:31,238 --> 00:40:32,106
Nice!

836
00:40:32,706 --> 00:40:34,875
- Nice smack!
- Smack!

837
00:40:35,142 --> 00:40:37,077
Smack!

838
00:40:37,978 --> 00:40:41,155
(Myoung Hwa penetrating the center
like the archipuncture.)

839
00:40:41,156 --> 00:40:43,325
- Myoung Hwa, nice.
- You too, Na Yeon.

840
00:40:44,084 --> 00:40:46,253
Compared to
when she just joined Wonder Dogs,

841
00:40:46,253 --> 00:40:48,055
she's five times faster now.

842
00:40:48,321 --> 00:40:51,257
She used to be slower
like "Moon, Myoung, Hwa," but look.

843
00:40:52,159 --> 00:40:53,193
"Fast Myoung Hwa!"

844
00:40:54,895 --> 00:40:57,898
I told you they'd try a quick attack.

845
00:40:58,432 --> 00:40:59,633
Nice!

846
00:40:59,633 --> 00:41:01,502
(Middle blocker is offense too.)

847
00:41:02,269 --> 00:41:04,371
(Myoung Hwa evolving)

848
00:41:04,371 --> 00:41:06,139
(First, Serving Queen)

849
00:41:06,707 --> 00:41:10,444
(Next, Wall Myoung Hwa)

850
00:41:11,144 --> 00:41:14,848
(Followed by Defense Myoung Hwa)

851
00:41:15,916 --> 00:41:17,818
(And Defense Myoung Hwa evolves into...)

852
00:41:18,685 --> 00:41:21,788
(Quick Myoung Hwa of fast attacks.)

853
00:41:22,222 --> 00:41:25,058
Na Yeon, keep it going.
Just send it to the middle.

854
00:41:25,859 --> 00:41:29,229
Wonder Dogs are widening the gap
by two points with middle quick attacks.

855
00:41:31,565 --> 00:41:34,568
(They need to widen the gap more.)

856
00:41:36,703 --> 00:41:39,339
A free ball. Myoung Hwa. Na Yeon.

857
00:41:39,339 --> 00:41:40,240
Enkhsoyol!

858
00:41:41,041 --> 00:41:42,476
Darn it.

859
00:41:43,243 --> 00:41:44,377
Enkhsoyol's faint tip.

860
00:41:44,377 --> 00:41:46,145
(Ball goes straight to opponent's libero.)

861
00:41:46,413 --> 00:41:48,081
(Lost a free-ball chance)

862
00:41:48,982 --> 00:41:50,417
- Da Bin!
- It works.

863
00:41:50,417 --> 00:41:52,452
(Da Bin took the chance and scored.)

864
00:41:52,986 --> 00:41:54,054
Let's go!

865
00:41:54,488 --> 00:41:56,122
Enkhsoyol, don't aim it there.

866
00:41:56,122 --> 00:41:57,256
That's where their libero is.

867
00:41:58,592 --> 00:42:00,827
Enkhsoyol, how did I tell you to hit?

868
00:42:01,562 --> 00:42:02,595
Straight ahead...

869
00:42:03,029 --> 00:42:05,732
- Hit it straight.
- Okay, Coach.

870
00:42:05,732 --> 00:42:08,435
It's a shame that
we tend to waste our free-ball chances.

871
00:42:08,668 --> 00:42:09,871
One-point difference, nine to ten.

872
00:42:09,872 --> 00:42:10,904
(Their error, other teams' chance)

873
00:42:12,139 --> 00:42:13,473
Let's go!

874
00:42:13,473 --> 00:42:14,774
(Da Bin is on a roll.)

875
00:42:15,609 --> 00:42:17,044
- Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

876
00:42:18,178 --> 00:42:20,146
(Eun Ji is serving?)

877
00:42:20,146 --> 00:42:22,348
Turn left, guys. Enkhsoyol too.

878
00:42:23,016 --> 00:42:24,284
Turn left, guys.

879
00:42:24,284 --> 00:42:25,652
(Turning their body for Eun Ji's serve)

880
00:42:25,952 --> 00:42:26,686
Serve.

881
00:42:30,023 --> 00:42:31,458
Enkhsoyol set it up well.

882
00:42:31,791 --> 00:42:32,558
Hit it!

883
00:42:32,959 --> 00:42:33,826
A face-to-face battle.

884
00:42:33,827 --> 00:42:37,698
(Will it work this time?)

885
00:42:39,032 --> 00:42:41,234
(Da Bin's national-team-level dig)

886
00:42:41,234 --> 00:42:42,235
Their defense is shaky.

887
00:42:42,235 --> 00:42:43,436
(Ready for the set-up)

888
00:42:43,436 --> 00:42:44,604
Watch the front!

889
00:42:47,207 --> 00:42:47,941
Ho Bin.

890
00:42:47,941 --> 00:42:49,109
Yes!

891
00:42:49,643 --> 00:42:50,610
Nice!

892
00:42:50,610 --> 00:42:52,245
- Let's go!
- Nice.

893
00:42:54,748 --> 00:42:58,285
(Middle blocker taken down
by middle blocker)

894
00:42:59,386 --> 00:43:01,488
My mistake.

895
00:43:03,056 --> 00:43:04,791
It wasn't even a strong one.

896
00:43:05,492 --> 00:43:07,994
Red Sparks are using the middle too.

897
00:43:09,095 --> 00:43:13,599
Their play is pretty straightforward.
They don't have middle attacks.

898
00:43:15,235 --> 00:43:19,839
(But they did, unexpectedly.)

899
00:43:21,239 --> 00:43:23,173
(Ko Hee Jin, former middle blocker's
countermove.)

900
00:43:24,371 --> 00:43:28,508
(The center battle just breaks out.)

901
00:43:29,743 --> 00:43:30,743
(The battle of middle blockers)

902
00:43:30,743 --> 00:43:32,712
The battle at the center is heating up!

903
00:43:34,180 --> 00:43:37,884
Myoung Hwa. Why would you allow
their middle blocker to score?

904
00:43:38,318 --> 00:43:40,153
I know!

905
00:43:40,253 --> 00:43:42,288
- Did you let her because she's a middle?
- No.

906
00:43:42,522 --> 00:43:45,058
It's not even a wide range.
Why let them score?

907
00:43:46,659 --> 00:43:48,261
Watch net violation!

908
00:43:48,261 --> 00:43:49,128
Nice and calm.

909
00:43:49,128 --> 00:43:50,529
(Ho Bin, Myoung Hwa, middle blockers)

910
00:43:51,464 --> 00:43:53,032
It's a tie, 10 to 10.

911
00:43:53,700 --> 00:43:54,501
Serve.

912
00:43:54,501 --> 00:43:55,936
(Eun Ji serving)

913
00:43:57,637 --> 00:43:58,504
Hye In.

914
00:43:58,872 --> 00:44:00,540
It's set up high, very fast.

915
00:44:00,940 --> 00:44:01,841
Hit it!

916
00:44:02,142 --> 00:44:03,777
They changed the direction
and sent it over.

917
00:44:04,444 --> 00:44:05,612
She hits it with her fist.

918
00:44:06,212 --> 00:44:07,947
What are you guys doing?

919
00:44:08,515 --> 00:44:09,483
My ball!

920
00:44:09,783 --> 00:44:10,850
Don't rush.

921
00:44:15,922 --> 00:44:17,290
(While the opponents are
down on the floor,)

922
00:44:17,290 --> 00:44:20,994
(she commands A quick attack.)

923
00:44:23,396 --> 00:44:25,064
(It's Quick Myoung Hwa's time.)

924
00:44:25,064 --> 00:44:28,640
She's smart, good at studying,
and diligent,

925
00:44:28,641 --> 00:44:29,321
but she's slow.

926
00:44:29,369 --> 00:44:31,404
(Myoung Hwa is slow, you'd say?)

927
00:44:32,539 --> 00:44:35,074
(Maybe you couldn't see her
because she's too fast.)

928
00:44:35,074 --> 00:44:36,275
She's so fast.

929
00:44:36,276 --> 00:44:37,611
Myoung Hwa!

930
00:44:39,546 --> 00:44:42,248
Middle quick attack!

931
00:44:42,248 --> 00:44:43,516
Nice signaling.

932
00:44:43,516 --> 00:44:46,419
Nice attack!

933
00:44:46,753 --> 00:44:47,620
Myoung Hwa is on fire.

934
00:44:49,455 --> 00:44:51,857
(Quick Myoung Hwa wins the center battle.)

935
00:44:51,858 --> 00:44:52,759
Sorry.

936
00:44:57,230 --> 00:45:00,233
The opponent fell,
and the center was empty.

937
00:45:00,400 --> 00:45:01,568
Man.

938
00:45:02,335 --> 00:45:05,772
Myoung Hwa takes a step forward
in this fierce center battle.

939
00:45:06,806 --> 00:45:09,942
(Getting ready to serve,
looking like a general)

940
00:45:10,343 --> 00:45:11,911
Now, when Myoung Hwa is serving,

941
00:45:11,911 --> 00:45:14,947
- everyone has high expectations.
- Of course.

942
00:45:16,483 --> 00:45:20,053
(I'll serve it right to the middle too.)

943
00:45:20,787 --> 00:45:21,588
Eun Ji.

944
00:45:22,789 --> 00:45:25,091
(Today's...)

945
00:45:25,091 --> 00:45:27,293
(Quick Myoung Hwa's day.)

946
00:45:28,094 --> 00:45:29,228
Darn it!

947
00:45:30,497 --> 00:45:32,399
Oh, no. It hit the net.

948
00:45:34,834 --> 00:45:36,235
(Trying not to laugh)

949
00:45:36,235 --> 00:45:38,237
Let's go. Let's do one more.

950
00:45:39,239 --> 00:45:40,674
- Let's go.
- Sorry.

951
00:45:43,009 --> 00:45:46,346
Hey, what's wrong with your serve?

952
00:45:46,346 --> 00:45:47,247
(Shaking head)

953
00:45:48,081 --> 00:45:51,050
(Because of Quick Myoung Hwa's
serve error,)

954
00:45:51,050 --> 00:45:52,752
(the score is now tied.)

955
00:45:52,752 --> 00:45:53,920
It's 11 to 11.

956
00:45:55,722 --> 00:45:56,823
Stay focused!

957
00:45:56,823 --> 00:45:57,957
(They both need to focus.)

958
00:45:57,957 --> 00:45:59,192
Stay in your position.

959
00:46:00,093 --> 00:46:00,927
Serve.

960
00:46:01,427 --> 00:46:03,629
(Da Bin's serve)

961
00:46:04,864 --> 00:46:05,698
My ball!

962
00:46:05,765 --> 00:46:07,100
Enkhsoyol.

963
00:46:07,100 --> 00:46:08,267
Go! Hit it!

964
00:46:08,267 --> 00:46:09,235
She sprints!

965
00:46:09,235 --> 00:46:10,737
(Enkhsoyol's spike)

966
00:46:11,337 --> 00:46:12,271
Oh, no.

967
00:46:14,674 --> 00:46:15,475
Hit it!

968
00:46:16,075 --> 00:46:16,976
Seon Ok hit it.

969
00:46:16,976 --> 00:46:18,644
- Seung Ju is in the back.
- Na Yeon, go. Slowly.

970
00:46:18,645 --> 00:46:19,679
With power.

971
00:46:19,746 --> 00:46:20,647
Let's go!

972
00:46:20,647 --> 00:46:21,948
(It's too far.)

973
00:46:22,549 --> 00:46:25,252
(It's not a good toss.)

974
00:46:27,020 --> 00:46:30,056
(An attack error out of bounds)

975
00:46:31,991 --> 00:46:33,159
That's not how you should hit.

976
00:46:33,893 --> 00:46:34,827
Look at it now.

977
00:46:35,061 --> 00:46:37,463
You can run and hit all you want.
It'll never work.

978
00:46:43,303 --> 00:46:44,170
My mistake.

979
00:46:44,837 --> 00:46:47,506
Enkhsoyol, how do you hit a ball
that's not good?

980
00:46:48,207 --> 00:46:50,009
Hit it straight!

981
00:46:50,677 --> 00:46:52,311
Don't make an error, Enkhsoyol.
It was doable.

982
00:46:52,311 --> 00:46:53,612
- Okay.
- Let's go right away.

983
00:46:54,080 --> 00:46:56,149
The Red Sparks are now leading
by one point.

984
00:46:56,149 --> 00:46:57,117
It's 12 to 11.

985
00:46:58,685 --> 00:47:00,053
(The tight battle continues.)

986
00:47:00,053 --> 00:47:01,454
- Grab it!
- Hit it!

987
00:47:01,654 --> 00:47:03,889
Seon Ok versus Hye In!

988
00:47:04,457 --> 00:47:05,324
Na Yeon.

989
00:47:07,260 --> 00:47:08,661
Please set it close!

990
00:47:12,498 --> 00:47:14,100
It's blocked. Seo Hyun.

991
00:47:14,100 --> 00:47:15,668
(Red Sparks' offense chance)

992
00:47:15,902 --> 00:47:17,470
(Getting ready to block right away)

993
00:47:17,637 --> 00:47:18,538
Spike!

994
00:47:22,742 --> 00:47:23,910
It's a block-out.

995
00:47:27,246 --> 00:47:29,949
(A rushed set gives away
their attacking chance)

996
00:47:31,284 --> 00:47:32,118
Sorry, Seung Ju.

997
00:47:32,719 --> 00:47:34,320
You can do it!

998
00:47:34,320 --> 00:47:37,456
When Na Yeon receives the ball...

999
00:47:37,457 --> 00:47:41,294
that's a bit off,
her set tends to get a bit shaky.

1000
00:47:41,294 --> 00:47:43,062
- That's right.
- Enkhsoyol, please. Darn it!

1001
00:47:43,062 --> 00:47:44,931
(Mental breakdown)

1002
00:47:45,632 --> 00:47:47,400
Too many shaky sets right now.

1003
00:47:47,400 --> 00:47:49,649
(Deep in thought)

1004
00:47:52,568 --> 00:47:54,136
Sol.

1005
00:47:57,867 --> 00:48:00,269
- Should I go in? Right now?
- Yes, go on in.

1006
00:48:02,037 --> 00:48:05,307
(Sol is back in court.)

1007
00:48:05,399 --> 00:48:09,465
They changed setters.
Na Yeon came out, and Sol went in.

1008
00:48:09,652 --> 00:48:10,725
Sol.

1009
00:48:10,726 --> 00:48:14,683
It's a high ball right now.

1010
00:48:14,684 --> 00:48:16,226
(High ball: A high ball
for the setter to work with)

1011
00:48:16,251 --> 00:48:18,587
(To clear a high ball,)

1012
00:48:19,355 --> 00:48:20,879
(Sol, the tall setter, is chosen.)

1013
00:48:20,880 --> 00:48:23,826
I'd love to hear that I've improved
since my time with Red Sparks.

1014
00:48:24,524 --> 00:48:25,993
You're good, Sol. You can do it!

1015
00:48:27,329 --> 00:48:29,996
They'd need to make the most
of the tall setter's advantage.

1016
00:48:30,400 --> 00:48:32,802
(Will the coach's substitution pay off?)

1017
00:48:34,005 --> 00:48:35,105
A serve by Seo Hyun.

1018
00:48:37,245 --> 00:48:38,676
Song Hee receives it.

1019
00:48:40,244 --> 00:48:42,991
- They'll need to handle the toss well.
- Get it.

1020
00:48:45,945 --> 00:48:48,418
Seung Ju connects it to a point.

1021
00:48:49,799 --> 00:48:51,171
Block higher.

1022
00:48:53,071 --> 00:48:55,626
For the setter,

1023
00:48:55,664 --> 00:48:57,294
the very first set
after coming in is huge.

1024
00:48:57,295 --> 00:49:01,331
Whether it leads to a point
makes a big difference.

1025
00:49:02,556 --> 00:49:05,630
You should place it accurately
not to make them happen.

1026
00:49:05,689 --> 00:49:08,339
(Dominating their opponent
and leading by one point again)

1027
00:49:08,351 --> 00:49:10,707
The score is 14 to 15.
They're ahead by a point.

1028
00:49:11,909 --> 00:49:14,011
(Serve by Hyeon Jeong)

1029
00:49:18,620 --> 00:49:19,620
Eun Ji spikes it.

1030
00:49:21,251 --> 00:49:23,753
That was a smart and bold move.

1031
00:49:23,754 --> 00:49:25,689
(Red Sparks close the gap right away.)

1032
00:49:25,690 --> 00:49:28,593
In the third set,
Eun Ji's hitting percentage is...

1033
00:49:28,594 --> 00:49:31,161
- getting back on track.
- Indeed.

1034
00:49:31,695 --> 00:49:33,530
(When they get ahead by one point,)

1035
00:49:33,797 --> 00:49:36,366
(the other side catches up right away.)

1036
00:49:36,597 --> 00:49:39,603
The Wonder Dogs and Red Sparks are
trading points.

1037
00:49:40,168 --> 00:49:43,107
No one can predict
how this match will turn out.

1038
00:49:44,077 --> 00:49:45,238
The score is tied at 15 to 15.

1039
00:49:51,454 --> 00:49:52,649
Will it go over the net?

1040
00:49:52,650 --> 00:49:54,818
(It's too high up.)

1041
00:50:00,224 --> 00:50:01,692
(Going straight to a quick attack)

1042
00:50:01,892 --> 00:50:03,393
(Shouting with joy)

1043
00:50:03,522 --> 00:50:04,895
Thank you.

1044
00:50:05,329 --> 00:50:06,630
(Smiling)

1045
00:50:07,464 --> 00:50:09,232
(The ball is right off the net,)

1046
00:50:09,466 --> 00:50:11,401
(and she just reaches with her arm
and pops it over.)

1047
00:50:11,802 --> 00:50:13,771
(This is the class of a tall setter.)

1048
00:50:14,071 --> 00:50:16,073
(That's the one.)

1049
00:50:16,109 --> 00:50:18,702
The second technical timeout.

1050
00:50:18,703 --> 00:50:20,336
Come here, guys.

1051
00:50:21,009 --> 00:50:23,080
If Eun Ji attacks this time,

1052
00:50:23,448 --> 00:50:26,349
block it with your right hand.
You won't miss it again, right?

1053
00:50:26,650 --> 00:50:29,253
(They promised to block from the center.)

1054
00:50:30,053 --> 00:50:33,657
(But Eun Ji kept scoring
through a block touch-out.)

1055
00:50:34,057 --> 00:50:36,927
(The rookie coach's plan to get ahead)

1056
00:50:37,818 --> 00:50:39,896
A line attack.

1057
00:50:39,897 --> 00:50:41,331
(A right-hand block set for the line shot)

1058
00:50:41,641 --> 00:50:45,302
- Where do you keep the ball?
- On the right side.

1059
00:50:47,070 --> 00:50:49,933
(An on-the-spot adjustment
to the blocking strategy)

1060
00:50:49,973 --> 00:50:51,740
They need to win in the third set...

1061
00:50:51,900 --> 00:50:54,911
- for the players to gain more confidence.
- Indeed.

1062
00:50:56,413 --> 00:51:00,050
(Now is the moment to widen the gap.)

1063
00:51:00,712 --> 00:51:01,919
A serve by Sol.

1064
00:51:07,357 --> 00:51:08,517
(Easily)

1065
00:51:08,518 --> 00:51:10,577
It's blocked on the left,
and she pushes it over.

1066
00:51:11,512 --> 00:51:12,512
She keeps the ball alive.

1067
00:51:12,687 --> 00:51:13,831
- And Eun Ji.
- Hit it!

1068
00:51:13,832 --> 00:51:16,066
It's coming. Get it, Myoung Hwa.

1069
00:51:17,963 --> 00:51:21,305
Eun Ji's ball will come
to the right side this time.

1070
00:51:24,207 --> 00:51:27,310
(It touches her right hand.)

1071
00:51:27,778 --> 00:51:29,880
(It goes straight
into the other team's court.)

1072
00:51:30,347 --> 00:51:32,549
(What a successful blocking!)

1073
00:51:33,130 --> 00:51:34,217
I missed.

1074
00:51:36,453 --> 00:51:38,221
(We actually did it.)

1075
00:51:39,089 --> 00:51:41,825
(There we go.)

1076
00:51:44,362 --> 00:51:46,697
It worked right away.

1077
00:51:49,374 --> 00:51:50,667
Manager Boo has grown...

1078
00:51:50,914 --> 00:51:53,593
enough to give Coach Yeon Kyoung
a high-five.

1079
00:51:53,594 --> 00:51:57,808
Manager Boo just proved that he is
the manager for Wonder Dogs.

1080
00:52:01,812 --> 00:52:03,781
(Another serve by Sol)

1081
00:52:05,349 --> 00:52:06,625
(It's a powerful serve.)

1082
00:52:06,626 --> 00:52:08,892
- Seo Hyun. Their timing is off.
- Hey.

1083
00:52:09,325 --> 00:52:11,137
Free ball for the Wonder Dogs.

1084
00:52:12,282 --> 00:52:13,282
Sol's toss.

1085
00:52:13,924 --> 00:52:15,359
(Seung Ju soars.)

1086
00:52:16,569 --> 00:52:19,216
Seung Ju scores!

1087
00:52:21,732 --> 00:52:24,001
(Shouting with joy)

1088
00:52:24,301 --> 00:52:27,070
(The Wonder Dogs are ahead
by three points.)

1089
00:52:28,807 --> 00:52:30,173
Good job.

1090
00:52:30,941 --> 00:52:31,775
(A high-five)

1091
00:52:33,343 --> 00:52:35,445
(Atta girl!)

1092
00:52:35,812 --> 00:52:37,781
(First, they changed the setter to Sol.)

1093
00:52:38,181 --> 00:52:40,183
(Then,
by changing their blocking strategy,)

1094
00:52:40,884 --> 00:52:44,788
(the Wonder Dogs turned the tide
in their favor.)

1095
00:52:45,422 --> 00:52:47,958
(On the other hand)

1096
00:52:52,462 --> 00:52:58,201
(Coach Hee Jin took off
to a relaxed start.)

1097
00:53:01,037 --> 00:53:03,506
(He was happy in the first set.)

1098
00:53:05,075 --> 00:53:07,778
(He got angry in the second set.)

1099
00:53:08,145 --> 00:53:09,780
(And now, in the third set,)

1100
00:53:11,248 --> 00:53:15,085
(he went quite.)

1101
00:53:16,853 --> 00:53:19,656
(Ask for a timeout.)

1102
00:53:20,557 --> 00:53:25,061
(Red Sparks, timeout)

1103
00:53:25,484 --> 00:53:27,677
- You're not controlling the ball at all.
- Yes, Coach.

1104
00:53:32,436 --> 00:53:36,273
(On an eggshell)

1105
00:53:39,242 --> 00:53:40,810
Is volleyball that hard for you?

1106
00:53:43,375 --> 00:53:48,127
Everything gets tough
because you're not doing your part.

1107
00:53:49,647 --> 00:53:51,554
Don't think of anything else.

1108
00:53:51,927 --> 00:53:55,266
Just focus on what you have to do
in your positions.

1109
00:53:55,267 --> 00:53:58,595
When the six of you do that,
you can play good volleyball.

1110
00:53:59,292 --> 00:54:03,005
- Why are you not playing as a team?
- Let's go for it!

1111
00:54:05,151 --> 00:54:08,038
The score is 15 to 18.
The Wonder Dogs are 3 points ahead.

1112
00:54:08,878 --> 00:54:11,908
(Serve by Sol)

1113
00:54:21,585 --> 00:54:23,087
(Da Bin spikes.)

1114
00:54:25,582 --> 00:54:28,191
(It's another block touch out.)

1115
00:54:28,320 --> 00:54:29,826
She braced herself and spiked.

1116
00:54:33,946 --> 00:54:36,939
Oh, my goodness.

1117
00:54:39,729 --> 00:54:43,005
- Her own hand!
- It's not going as she wants.

1118
00:54:43,491 --> 00:54:44,910
Don't spread your fingers.

1119
00:54:45,264 --> 00:54:47,157
If you lean forward,
they'll block for you.

1120
00:54:48,278 --> 00:54:51,281
(Serve by Ye Rim)

1121
00:54:53,629 --> 00:54:54,629
I'm sorry.

1122
00:54:54,784 --> 00:54:57,954
(With a shaky pass,
they just manage to push it over.)

1123
00:54:59,723 --> 00:55:01,158
(A surprise quick attack down the middle)

1124
00:55:03,927 --> 00:55:05,162
(She pulled off a pancake.)

1125
00:55:07,307 --> 00:55:08,665
That's a relief.

1126
00:55:08,666 --> 00:55:11,368
(Red Sparks' free ball)

1127
00:55:11,868 --> 00:55:14,304
(Da Bin hits.)

1128
00:55:15,706 --> 00:55:18,208
It's a block out again.

1129
00:55:18,209 --> 00:55:21,078
(A point off the blocker's hands)

1130
00:55:22,003 --> 00:55:23,823
The score is 18 to 17.
They're 1 point apart.

1131
00:55:25,782 --> 00:55:28,184
Da Bin is really striking the ball well.

1132
00:55:29,920 --> 00:55:33,624
(A strong spike
that gets through Wall Myoung Hwa)

1133
00:55:37,561 --> 00:55:40,397
(The one who wants to block)

1134
00:55:40,430 --> 00:55:44,067
(The one who wants to get through)

1135
00:55:44,668 --> 00:55:50,607
(The battle between the sword
and shield continues.)

1136
00:55:53,510 --> 00:55:54,999
- Mine.
- Hyo Seo.

1137
00:55:55,000 --> 00:55:56,213
It's a short receive.

1138
00:55:57,247 --> 00:55:59,149
- She blocked it right away.
- Mine.

1139
00:55:59,716 --> 00:56:01,484
(Da Bi has the ball again.)

1140
00:56:02,052 --> 00:56:05,155
(I'm definitely blocking this one.)

1141
00:56:07,691 --> 00:56:10,227
(But the block didn't hold.)

1142
00:56:11,143 --> 00:56:13,303
Myong Hwa pulled off her arms!

1143
00:56:13,863 --> 00:56:15,832
(Actually, Myoung Hwa...)

1144
00:56:16,202 --> 00:56:18,069
I'll let go of Da Bin's balls on purpose.

1145
00:56:20,604 --> 00:56:23,740
(Tactical not-blocking)

1146
00:56:24,140 --> 00:56:26,776
(Wise Myoung Hwa)

1147
00:56:26,812 --> 00:56:29,345
Myoung Hwa!

1148
00:56:29,412 --> 00:56:32,282
We love you, Myoung Hwa!

1149
00:56:33,149 --> 00:56:35,385
(Finally out of the block touch out rut)

1150
00:56:35,524 --> 00:56:37,498
- That was a good move.
- Nice one!

1151
00:56:37,954 --> 00:56:40,523
(Proud)

1152
00:56:42,058 --> 00:56:44,594
(Third set, Red Sparks 17
: Wonder Dogs 20)

1153
00:56:47,263 --> 00:56:49,265
(Serve by Seung Ju)

1154
00:56:50,867 --> 00:56:52,502
(A shaky receive)

1155
00:56:52,575 --> 00:56:53,575
A quick attack.

1156
00:56:54,881 --> 00:56:56,373
That was dangerous.

1157
00:56:58,728 --> 00:57:00,043
Song Hee.

1158
00:57:01,911 --> 00:57:02,911
That's Eun Ji.

1159
00:57:02,912 --> 00:57:05,448
(This time, it's Eun Ji.)

1160
00:57:08,918 --> 00:57:11,921
(Blocking successfully)

1161
00:57:12,078 --> 00:57:14,024
Enkhsoyol!

1162
00:57:15,258 --> 00:57:18,094
(Nice block!)

1163
00:57:22,532 --> 00:57:22,999
Shoot.

1164
00:57:25,255 --> 00:57:26,469
I missed.

1165
00:57:27,122 --> 00:57:30,306
The score is 21 to 17.
They're 4 points apart.

1166
00:57:31,207 --> 00:57:34,811
(Third straight serve by Seung Ju)

1167
00:57:39,983 --> 00:57:41,384
(Their defense crumbles.)

1168
00:57:42,532 --> 00:57:43,532
She sent the ball over the net.

1169
00:57:44,625 --> 00:57:46,589
Sol should stay calm.

1170
00:57:47,776 --> 00:57:49,459
(A quick back toss)

1171
00:57:49,894 --> 00:57:51,994
(They're late.)

1172
00:57:52,328 --> 00:57:55,161
(The leap of the little giant)

1173
00:57:56,228 --> 00:57:57,428
Han Song Hee!

1174
00:57:57,428 --> 00:58:00,228
It lands inside the court!

1175
00:58:01,928 --> 00:58:03,928
(Nice toss!)

1176
00:58:04,361 --> 00:58:06,861
(We're on a winning streak!)

1177
00:58:07,094 --> 00:58:08,094
Nice.

1178
00:58:12,128 --> 00:58:13,728
Get to your places!

1179
00:58:16,628 --> 00:58:17,694
I was proud of them.

1180
00:58:17,694 --> 00:58:21,028
Our players knew what to do
when they played.

1181
00:58:21,028 --> 00:58:25,861
I constantly felt that we're improving...

1182
00:58:25,861 --> 00:58:27,594
because of that.

1183
00:58:28,728 --> 00:58:30,294
Their play worked flawlessly.

1184
00:58:30,294 --> 00:58:32,328
And every player did great.

1185
00:58:32,328 --> 00:58:33,394
(Third set, Red Sparks 17
: Wonder Dogs 22)

1186
00:58:36,228 --> 00:58:38,561
In 1, 2, 3. Nice serve!

1187
00:58:40,694 --> 00:58:41,894
Nice serve!

1188
00:58:41,894 --> 00:58:42,894
It shook their position.

1189
00:58:43,594 --> 00:58:46,461
(They rush to set the ball up.)

1190
00:58:46,928 --> 00:58:49,328
Enkhsoyol receives Jeon Da Bin's tip.

1191
00:58:49,961 --> 00:58:52,061
(Where will she toss the ball?)

1192
00:58:52,494 --> 00:58:54,361
Pipe.

1193
00:58:55,128 --> 00:58:58,161
(It's a back attack this time!)

1194
00:58:58,928 --> 00:59:01,661
(Throughout the match
against the Red Sparks,)

1195
00:59:01,661 --> 00:59:05,094
(she pointed out the use
of back attack in the middle.)

1196
00:59:05,428 --> 00:59:06,428
(That's it.)

1197
00:59:09,894 --> 00:59:11,228
A back attack in the middle!

1198
00:59:11,228 --> 00:59:13,328
Pyo Seung Ju scores with a blockout!

1199
00:59:17,594 --> 00:59:18,961
Great attack!

1200
00:59:21,594 --> 00:59:24,061
Enkhsoyol, Han Song Hee, and Pyo Seung Ju.

1201
00:59:24,061 --> 00:59:26,061
Left, right, and middle.

1202
00:59:26,061 --> 00:59:27,661
They attack from everywhere.

1203
00:59:27,661 --> 00:59:28,694
You're right.

1204
00:59:30,928 --> 00:59:32,561
It's 23 to 17.

1205
00:59:32,561 --> 00:59:34,828
- Against the pro team,
- Okay.

1206
00:59:34,828 --> 00:59:36,261
they're leading by six points.

1207
00:59:37,294 --> 00:59:42,428
(We can't lose like this.)

1208
00:59:42,428 --> 00:59:45,094
(We'll beat them this way.)

1209
00:59:45,261 --> 00:59:46,561
Two more points!

1210
00:59:46,561 --> 00:59:47,661
(The third set will be
their turning point.)

1211
00:59:47,928 --> 00:59:49,761
(Who will seize the victory?)

1212
00:59:49,761 --> 00:59:50,861
In 1, 2, 3.

1213
00:59:50,861 --> 00:59:52,161
Nice serve!

1214
00:59:52,161 --> 00:59:53,328
(Pyo Seung Ju serves.)

1215
00:59:55,161 --> 00:59:56,428
It hits the net!

1216
00:59:57,894 --> 01:00:00,528
(Shin Eun Ji, the ace, spikes.)

1217
01:00:04,694 --> 01:00:06,894
- That was a nice defense.
- She saved the ball.

1218
01:00:06,894 --> 01:00:09,694
(Tossing to Enkhsoyol)

1219
01:00:10,494 --> 01:00:12,494
Enkhsoyol spikes!

1220
01:00:14,561 --> 01:00:16,594
A block out!

1221
01:00:18,928 --> 01:00:20,994
(They fail to defend.)

1222
01:00:20,994 --> 01:00:21,994
Come on.

1223
01:00:24,228 --> 01:00:26,628
- I'm sorry.
- I'll do it.

1224
01:00:27,928 --> 01:00:29,761
I feel dizzy, Gang Ju.

1225
01:00:30,528 --> 01:00:31,928
I can't believe it!

1226
01:00:31,928 --> 01:00:33,594
It's 24 to 17.

1227
01:00:34,294 --> 01:00:37,294
It's now the Wonder Dogs' set point.

1228
01:00:37,528 --> 01:00:39,394
(Instructing the target area)

1229
01:00:39,394 --> 01:00:40,428
Yes!

1230
01:00:45,094 --> 01:00:46,328
(A shaky reception)

1231
01:00:46,994 --> 01:00:47,994
Go!

1232
01:00:48,294 --> 01:00:49,394
Lee Ho Bin attacks in the middle!

1233
01:00:51,228 --> 01:00:53,461
- Nice defense!
- Pyo Seung Ju saved it.

1234
01:00:54,194 --> 01:00:55,894
(Enkhsoyol prepares to attack.)

1235
01:00:56,894 --> 01:00:58,628
It's one block, Enkhsoyol!

1236
01:00:58,861 --> 01:01:00,761
- All right!
- Nice toss!

1237
01:01:01,294 --> 01:01:03,728
(Strong Enkhsoyol enters.)

1238
01:01:04,994 --> 01:01:07,988
(Will her attack succeed again?)

1239
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:13,367
(A finishing blow)

1240
01:01:13,367 --> 01:01:16,500
Enkhsoyol spikes!

1241
01:01:16,500 --> 01:01:18,134
Is this really happening?

1242
01:01:18,134 --> 01:01:21,734
The Wonder Dogs won the third set!

1243
01:01:22,867 --> 01:01:26,867
(Enkhsoyol played the key role.)

1244
01:01:28,134 --> 01:01:29,134
(We won!)

1245
01:01:29,134 --> 01:01:30,434
Nice one, Enkhsoyol!

1246
01:01:32,667 --> 01:01:34,934
The Wonder Dogs players really did...

1247
01:01:34,934 --> 01:01:38,950
- an outstanding play to win the set.
- That's right.

1248
01:01:38,950 --> 01:01:41,812
(Set score, Red Sparks 1: Wonder Dogs 2)

1249
01:01:42,053 --> 01:01:44,427
(Timeout for the fourth set)

1250
01:01:44,753 --> 01:01:48,719
Do you remember the course
I talked about on serving?

1251
01:01:48,719 --> 01:01:50,986
You should follow it exactly.

1252
01:01:50,986 --> 01:01:52,619
None of your serves worked.

1253
01:01:52,619 --> 01:01:56,786
(Their serve balls kept missing
the right course.)

1254
01:01:59,386 --> 01:02:02,286
(They lost crucial points
due to their errors.)

1255
01:02:02,853 --> 01:02:05,186
- Serve properly first.
- Yes, Coach.

1256
01:02:05,186 --> 01:02:06,453
Don't forget the basics
like serving and reception.

1257
01:02:06,453 --> 01:02:08,219
- Keep in line when Shin Eun Ji serves.
- Understood.

1258
01:02:08,219 --> 01:02:09,319
Align it with your right hand.

1259
01:02:09,719 --> 01:02:12,186
(Only one set left for the victory!)

1260
01:02:12,586 --> 01:02:14,486
(The team will survive
if they win this set.)

1261
01:02:14,853 --> 01:02:16,353
(The fateful fourth set)

1262
01:02:16,553 --> 01:02:18,086
(The match must be finished!)

1263
01:02:18,819 --> 01:02:21,319
The fourth set begins with Da Bin's serve.

1264
01:02:24,486 --> 01:02:25,953
C!

1265
01:02:26,386 --> 01:02:28,886
(It means tossing it deeply to Seung Ju.)

1266
01:02:29,586 --> 01:02:31,386
(She leaps high and spikes.)

1267
01:02:32,619 --> 01:02:34,586
Pyo Seung Ju scores!

1268
01:02:34,586 --> 01:02:36,819
(Captain Pyo gets the upper hand.)

1269
01:02:37,953 --> 01:02:40,053
(She precisely aims between blockers.)

1270
01:02:40,753 --> 01:02:42,753
(Sharply targeting the open spot)

1271
01:02:42,753 --> 01:02:45,919
Pyo Seung Ju looked exhausted
at the start of the game,

1272
01:02:45,919 --> 01:02:47,919
but now she's back
with the team's momentum.

1273
01:02:48,419 --> 01:02:50,919
The Wonder Dogs have a good start
with their first point.

1274
01:02:52,819 --> 01:02:54,819
(Gwak Seon Ok's reception)

1275
01:02:54,819 --> 01:02:55,819
She set it up.
Gwak Seon Ok!

1276
01:03:02,019 --> 01:03:03,453
(Koo Hye In's dive dig)

1277
01:03:03,719 --> 01:03:05,053
The ball is high in the air.

1278
01:03:05,053 --> 01:03:06,353
(Where will it go?)

1279
01:03:07,819 --> 01:03:10,319
(Out)

1280
01:03:10,553 --> 01:03:12,353
(That was so close!)

1281
01:03:13,286 --> 01:03:15,686
(It's okay. Nice defense.)

1282
01:03:15,686 --> 01:03:17,853
They may have missed a point,
but check her reaction speed.

1283
01:03:17,853 --> 01:03:19,819
- She was quite fast.
- Yes.

1284
01:03:19,819 --> 01:03:21,553
Watching the Wonder Dogs' game,

1285
01:03:21,553 --> 01:03:24,653
pro teams might think twice
about Koo Hye In.

1286
01:03:24,653 --> 01:03:26,153
- She stands out.
- Yes.

1287
01:03:26,819 --> 01:03:27,853
It's 1 to 1.

1288
01:03:27,853 --> 01:03:28,886
(Lee Ho Bin serves.)

1289
01:03:31,153 --> 01:03:33,686
Myoung Hwa, jump!

1290
01:03:33,686 --> 01:03:36,519
(Quick Myoung Hwa jumps!)

1291
01:03:37,686 --> 01:03:39,586
(A sudden quick from the middle)

1292
01:03:45,386 --> 01:03:46,519
That was an error.

1293
01:03:47,586 --> 01:03:49,286
(They distract the opponent again
with the quick attack.)

1294
01:03:49,286 --> 01:03:50,786
Thank you.

1295
01:03:52,886 --> 01:03:54,853
Ye Rim!

1296
01:03:54,853 --> 01:03:55,919
Can't you decide?

1297
01:03:56,819 --> 01:03:57,819
I can.

1298
01:03:59,919 --> 01:04:01,719
Even other players woke up...

1299
01:04:01,719 --> 01:04:04,419
by Captain Ko's fierce orders.

1300
01:04:04,419 --> 01:04:05,953
(Moon Myoung Hwa serves.)

1301
01:04:07,119 --> 01:04:08,119
Push it!

1302
01:04:08,119 --> 01:04:09,553
- Right!
- Hit it!

1303
01:04:09,553 --> 01:04:10,853
(A back toss to Shin Eun Ji)

1304
01:04:10,853 --> 01:04:12,586
(She rushes aggressively.)

1305
01:04:15,053 --> 01:04:17,119
Shin Eun Ji scores with a touchout.

1306
01:04:18,186 --> 01:04:21,086
Shin Eun Ji's spikes are quite powerful.

1307
01:04:21,086 --> 01:04:23,019
Where are you going, Na Yeon?

1308
01:04:23,319 --> 01:04:25,719
(Even a small mistake leads
to a loss of points.)

1309
01:04:26,686 --> 01:04:28,486
It's tied at two to two.
Shin Eun Ji serves.

1310
01:04:31,186 --> 01:04:32,186
Pyo Seung Ju.

1311
01:04:32,419 --> 01:04:33,453
Lee Na Yeon.

1312
01:04:33,453 --> 01:04:34,486
Enkhsoyol.

1313
01:04:34,653 --> 01:04:35,686
Enkhsoyol!

1314
01:04:35,686 --> 01:04:36,686
(Digging smoothly)

1315
01:04:36,686 --> 01:04:38,153
They defended it with a dig.

1316
01:04:38,153 --> 01:04:39,386
(Gwak Seon Ok's spike)

1317
01:04:39,386 --> 01:04:41,853
Gwak Seon Ok scores.

1318
01:04:42,319 --> 01:04:44,086
Gwak Seon Ok had
a 43 percent success rate...

1319
01:04:44,086 --> 01:04:45,753
on attacks during the third set.

1320
01:04:45,753 --> 01:04:46,753
She was strong.

1321
01:04:47,219 --> 01:04:48,753
(She's still formidable.)

1322
01:04:48,753 --> 01:04:51,886
It's 2 to 3, and the Red Sparks
lead with a single point.

1323
01:04:51,886 --> 01:04:54,619
Watch the short one
and the straight shot later.

1324
01:04:54,886 --> 01:04:56,619
One more point to tie, Enkhsoyol.

1325
01:04:57,786 --> 01:04:59,753
- Enkhsoyol.
- Look out for the short one.

1326
01:05:00,453 --> 01:05:02,186
(She sends a sign to Enkhsoyol.)

1327
01:05:05,953 --> 01:05:06,986
Serve.

1328
01:05:06,986 --> 01:05:07,986
(Shin Eun Ji serves.)

1329
01:05:09,586 --> 01:05:10,653
(The ball is sent high.)

1330
01:05:10,653 --> 01:05:11,819
Go!

1331
01:05:13,919 --> 01:05:15,853
(Enkhsoyol goes in.)

1332
01:05:16,053 --> 01:05:17,553
(Here she comes.)

1333
01:05:21,486 --> 01:05:23,253
That's it!

1334
01:05:23,253 --> 01:05:25,519
(It's not Enkhsoyol but Kim Hyeon Jeong!)

1335
01:05:25,519 --> 01:05:27,853
Middle quick attack!

1336
01:05:27,853 --> 01:05:30,353
They use quick attacks unexpectedly...

1337
01:05:30,353 --> 01:05:32,186
to make their opposing team confused.

1338
01:05:32,453 --> 01:05:34,419
Without looking at the middle,

1339
01:05:34,419 --> 01:05:38,286
An Ye Rim, the middle blocker, was
just about to leave.

1340
01:05:38,286 --> 01:05:41,419
- So she couldn't react to block at all.
- You're right.

1341
01:05:41,419 --> 01:05:44,019
Even if they attack from the left next,

1342
01:05:44,019 --> 01:05:45,753
An Ye Rim will watch the middle.

1343
01:05:45,753 --> 01:05:46,786
Of course.

1344
01:05:46,986 --> 01:05:49,086
(The score is tied again
thanks to their quicks at the middle.)

1345
01:05:50,019 --> 01:05:51,253
It's tied at 3 to 3.

1346
01:05:52,518 --> 01:05:54,484
(Tamira serves.)

1347
01:05:57,053 --> 01:05:58,853
(A powerful serve)

1348
01:06:00,519 --> 01:06:01,653
The reception is unstable.

1349
01:06:01,953 --> 01:06:03,619
(She quickly tosses.)

1350
01:06:05,953 --> 01:06:06,953
Gwak Seon Ok.

1351
01:06:06,953 --> 01:06:10,119
They blocked the ball. It's a point!

1352
01:06:10,119 --> 01:06:12,086
(Kim Hyeon Jeong scores twice in a row.)

1353
01:06:14,253 --> 01:06:16,553
(As the serve shook their reception,)

1354
01:06:17,053 --> 01:06:19,486
(Hyeon Jeong finishes easily
with a block.)

1355
01:06:20,153 --> 01:06:22,086
(She also breaks through
the defense with a quick attack...)

1356
01:06:22,753 --> 01:06:24,953
(as well as defending
with her solid block.)

1357
01:06:24,953 --> 01:06:26,686
(Kim Hyeon Jeong leads the flow.)

1358
01:06:27,786 --> 01:06:29,019
Great serve!

1359
01:06:30,619 --> 01:06:31,653
It's four to three.

1360
01:06:31,653 --> 01:06:32,853
(Fourth set, Red Sparks 3: Wonder Dogs 4)

1361
01:06:32,853 --> 01:06:34,819
(Tamira serves again.)

1362
01:06:36,653 --> 01:06:37,719
(Unstable again)

1363
01:06:37,719 --> 01:06:38,886
Jeon Da Bin's reception.

1364
01:06:38,886 --> 01:06:39,919
(A quick coverage)

1365
01:06:41,386 --> 01:06:42,419
Koo Hye In receives it.

1366
01:06:43,286 --> 01:06:44,286
Lee Na Yeon.

1367
01:06:45,691 --> 01:06:47,357
Enkhsoyol!

1368
01:06:47,757 --> 01:06:50,224
- Well done.
- That's how you do it.

1369
01:06:50,557 --> 01:06:52,291
(Fourth Set, Red Sparks 3 : Wonder Dogs 5)

1370
01:06:52,291 --> 01:06:54,991
The serve is good! Keep it up!

1371
01:06:55,924 --> 01:06:57,685
Tamira has been shaking the opponents...

1372
01:06:57,686 --> 01:06:59,724
with her serves
throughout the early fourth set.

1373
01:06:59,991 --> 01:07:02,424
(Holding it up)

1374
01:07:02,991 --> 01:07:04,157
Isn't this so cool?

1375
01:07:06,891 --> 01:07:07,891
Too short.

1376
01:07:08,557 --> 01:07:10,524
(Statue of Tamira)

1377
01:07:10,824 --> 01:07:12,657
(Zeroing the target)

1378
01:07:12,857 --> 01:07:13,857
(Fire!)

1379
01:07:15,291 --> 01:07:16,091
Nice serve.

1380
01:07:17,091 --> 01:07:18,924
(Tamira's spicy serve)

1381
01:07:24,624 --> 01:07:27,324
Enkhsoyol's block!

1382
01:07:27,924 --> 01:07:30,424
Tamira and Enkhsoyol show great teamwork!

1383
01:07:30,657 --> 01:07:31,824
Tamira set it up,

1384
01:07:31,824 --> 01:07:33,357
and Enkhsoyol finished it off.

1385
01:07:34,391 --> 01:07:36,291
The momentum is on our side.

1386
01:07:37,091 --> 01:07:39,124
(Nervous)

1387
01:07:40,257 --> 01:07:44,224
(Tamira's fourth serve in a row)

1388
01:07:54,224 --> 01:07:55,491
(Serve ace!)

1389
01:07:55,491 --> 01:07:56,857
It's in!

1390
01:07:56,857 --> 01:07:58,924
It landed perfectly in the corner!

1391
01:07:59,457 --> 01:08:01,591
Another point from her serve!

1392
01:08:02,057 --> 01:08:03,324
Nice!

1393
01:08:03,757 --> 01:08:06,157
(Even the Serving Queen saw that
it was good.)

1394
01:08:07,224 --> 01:08:08,991
Unbelievably impressive.

1395
01:08:10,257 --> 01:08:12,491
I want to show everything I've got.

1396
01:08:13,391 --> 01:08:16,491
Our team's new coach will be
Kim Yeon Koung.

1397
01:08:16,491 --> 01:08:18,291
(Upon hearing that her new coach
would be Yeon Koung,)

1398
01:08:18,991 --> 01:08:21,991
(this pure-hearted Mongolian girl
shed tears.)

1399
01:08:22,624 --> 01:08:25,557
(With her Mongolian friend Enkhsoyol,)

1400
01:08:26,457 --> 01:08:29,124
(she joined the team of her dreams.)

1401
01:08:31,124 --> 01:08:34,757
(But she has never gotten
a chance so far.)

1402
01:08:37,424 --> 01:08:40,824
(Watching her friend Enkhsoyol shine
on the court,)

1403
01:08:42,024 --> 01:08:45,591
(all she could do was support her team
from the bench...)

1404
01:08:46,191 --> 01:08:48,691
(waiting to be called someday.)

1405
01:08:50,257 --> 01:08:51,757
I know I can do it.

1406
01:08:52,224 --> 01:08:56,824
It'd be really nice
to be given another chance.

1407
01:08:58,057 --> 01:09:00,324
Still, if I try a little harder,

1408
01:09:00,324 --> 01:09:03,224
maybe I can be one
of the starting members.

1409
01:09:06,757 --> 01:09:09,057
(A chance will come to those
who are prepared.)

1410
01:09:09,591 --> 01:09:12,491
(She has never given up, not even once.)

1411
01:09:13,457 --> 01:09:14,357
That's it.

1412
01:09:14,924 --> 01:09:15,957
Darn it.

1413
01:09:17,324 --> 01:09:18,457
Nice serve.

1414
01:09:18,457 --> 01:09:19,991
Tamira, what's up with you today?

1415
01:09:20,657 --> 01:09:21,891
Did you have a nice lunch or something?

1416
01:09:21,891 --> 01:09:24,257
Eat the same thing every day.

1417
01:09:24,257 --> 01:09:28,091
Tamira's serving has been
great these days.

1418
01:09:28,091 --> 01:09:29,157
Technically, it could be a risk.

1419
01:09:29,991 --> 01:09:33,324
I think I'm going to bet on Tamira today.

1420
01:09:35,024 --> 01:09:36,524
(The new coach's new bet)

1421
01:09:36,991 --> 01:09:39,124
(It's time to prove myself.)

1422
01:09:45,391 --> 01:09:46,224
Nice serve.

1423
01:09:47,257 --> 01:09:49,257
(The ball rebounds high.)

1424
01:09:53,791 --> 01:09:57,757
(Direct kill)

1425
01:09:58,057 --> 01:10:00,891
(The Mongolian Duo is sweeping the court.)

1426
01:10:01,624 --> 01:10:03,324
(If you keep this up,)

1427
01:10:03,791 --> 01:10:06,024
(your chance will come.)

1428
01:10:06,991 --> 01:10:09,457
(Tamira's miraculous serve!)

1429
01:10:10,291 --> 01:10:11,224
I want to be good.

1430
01:10:11,224 --> 01:10:13,157
I want to show that I can do it.

1431
01:10:14,157 --> 01:10:15,957
Nice, Mongolians!

1432
01:10:17,191 --> 01:10:18,991
- Nice.
- Nice, Tamira.

1433
01:10:20,924 --> 01:10:23,291
You guys are too much today.

1434
01:10:25,091 --> 01:10:26,891
You want to retire and join them?

1435
01:10:28,991 --> 01:10:30,591
You're pros!

1436
01:10:30,591 --> 01:10:31,491
- Okay.
- Yes, Coach.

1437
01:10:31,857 --> 01:10:34,257
It's not me who should be upset right now.

1438
01:10:34,257 --> 01:10:35,191
It's you.

1439
01:10:35,191 --> 01:10:36,624
But you seem fine.

1440
01:10:36,624 --> 01:10:38,424
Only we, the coaching staff, are upset.

1441
01:10:38,424 --> 01:10:39,291
No.

1442
01:10:39,291 --> 01:10:41,957
It should be all of you who are enraged.

1443
01:10:41,957 --> 01:10:42,824
But look at you!

1444
01:10:42,824 --> 01:10:44,491
- You look so calm.
- No!

1445
01:10:44,491 --> 01:10:46,157
- Like a clam lake.
- No.

1446
01:10:46,157 --> 01:10:47,391
The game isn't over yet.

1447
01:10:47,391 --> 01:10:48,724
- No!
- No!

1448
01:10:48,724 --> 01:10:49,924
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1449
01:10:50,991 --> 01:10:52,191
Let's take it one at a time.

1450
01:10:53,557 --> 01:10:59,057
The Red Sparks' energy
has frozen like ice.

1451
01:10:59,324 --> 01:11:02,724
Enkhsoyol, I keep messing up
because I try to set it so high.

1452
01:11:02,724 --> 01:11:05,124
- I'll try not to think about it,
- I'll keep you in check.

1453
01:11:05,124 --> 01:11:07,191
- so keep me in check.
- Okay.

1454
01:11:07,191 --> 01:11:09,024
Serve! Focus!

1455
01:11:09,024 --> 01:11:10,691
(They dominated the early part
of the set against the pro team.)

1456
01:11:11,124 --> 01:11:12,391
It's 8 to 3.

1457
01:11:12,391 --> 01:11:14,291
The game resumes with Tamira's serve.

1458
01:11:14,691 --> 01:11:16,791
(Tamira's sixth serve)

1459
01:11:17,924 --> 01:11:18,824
Tamira.

1460
01:11:20,124 --> 01:11:21,991
(Seon Ok is ready to attack!)

1461
01:11:22,424 --> 01:11:24,357
(Seon Ok, you're a pro!)

1462
01:11:26,624 --> 01:11:29,024
(Touching)

1463
01:11:29,424 --> 01:11:31,324
(It breaks through!)

1464
01:11:32,457 --> 01:11:34,213
(This spiker is awakening.)

1465
01:11:34,214 --> 01:11:35,244
Seon Ok score with block out.

1466
01:11:36,257 --> 01:11:38,557
Coach Ko smiles again.

1467
01:11:39,524 --> 01:11:41,424
Even though we're leading,

1468
01:11:41,424 --> 01:11:43,557
it doesn't mean we can let our guard down.

1469
01:11:44,024 --> 01:11:46,524
Hyeon Jeong, watch out
for the short serve.

1470
01:11:47,724 --> 01:11:49,857
(Seon Ok's serve)

1471
01:11:52,091 --> 01:11:53,091
(Hyeon Jeong is thrown off.)

1472
01:11:53,091 --> 01:11:54,098
Hyeon Jeong saved it.

1473
01:11:54,099 --> 01:11:55,056
(Na Yeon tosses the ball...)

1474
01:11:55,057 --> 01:11:56,357
(to Enkhsoyol.)

1475
01:11:56,357 --> 01:11:57,857
Enkhsoyol.

1476
01:12:01,024 --> 01:12:02,224
The rally continues.

1477
01:12:02,224 --> 01:12:03,091
Seung Ju.

1478
01:12:06,124 --> 01:12:07,024
Jump and set!

1479
01:12:07,024 --> 01:12:08,624
Enkhsoyol!

1480
01:12:08,624 --> 01:12:09,891
Score!

1481
01:12:09,891 --> 01:12:15,057
Enkhsoyol is proving how capable
she is against a pro team!

1482
01:12:15,057 --> 01:12:17,357
Her strength isn't only
in spiking high balls.

1483
01:12:17,357 --> 01:12:20,924
She reads the play,
choosing between a short one...

1484
01:12:20,924 --> 01:12:23,757
and a quick one depending
on the situation.

1485
01:12:23,757 --> 01:12:27,524
This must be why Coach Kim
has been so tough on her.

1486
01:12:27,524 --> 01:12:30,191
Because Coach Kim saw her potential,

1487
01:12:30,191 --> 01:12:32,891
- Yes.
- she pushed her harder.

1488
01:12:32,891 --> 01:12:33,739
Serve!

1489
01:12:33,740 --> 01:12:35,224
(Improved Enkhsoyol's serve)

1490
01:12:35,991 --> 01:12:37,057
My mistake!

1491
01:12:37,257 --> 01:12:39,491
(Did we jinx it again?)

1492
01:12:40,691 --> 01:12:41,991
The serve was a bit low.

1493
01:12:41,991 --> 01:12:43,024
It goes over hastily.

1494
01:12:43,024 --> 01:12:44,124
(Where will Seo Hyun toss?)

1495
01:12:44,624 --> 01:12:45,624
It's A-quick!

1496
01:12:45,624 --> 01:12:47,257
That's it! C-quick!

1497
01:12:48,857 --> 01:12:49,757
Da Bin.

1498
01:12:50,224 --> 01:12:51,024
Blocked.

1499
01:12:51,024 --> 01:12:52,124
(They block it out once again.)

1500
01:12:53,457 --> 01:12:54,591
They're coming back.

1501
01:12:55,457 --> 01:12:57,024
(It's another c-quick.)

1502
01:12:57,557 --> 01:12:58,557
Spike.
It's out.

1503
01:12:59,457 --> 01:13:00,791
Sorry!

1504
01:13:01,357 --> 01:13:03,324
- Sorry!
- Darn it.

1505
01:13:03,324 --> 01:13:04,791
Hye In, where were you?

1506
01:13:04,791 --> 01:13:06,057
Sorry.

1507
01:13:06,057 --> 01:13:07,791
(Hye In failed to find the right spot.)

1508
01:13:08,924 --> 01:13:10,357
They're coming from the left.

1509
01:13:10,357 --> 01:13:11,691
It's 9 to 5. The gap is 4 points.

1510
01:13:11,691 --> 01:13:12,791
(Serve by Ye Rim)

1511
01:13:14,257 --> 01:13:15,091
Na Yeon.

1512
01:13:15,557 --> 01:13:17,457
(Hyeon Jeong's sudden quick attack)

1513
01:13:18,891 --> 01:13:19,857
Hyeon Jeong.

1514
01:13:19,857 --> 01:13:21,424
That's it. Score.

1515
01:13:21,424 --> 01:13:24,024
Wonder Dogs continue to lead.

1516
01:13:24,324 --> 01:13:25,991
(Nice job.)

1517
01:13:26,224 --> 01:13:27,724
(Na Yeon's serve)

1518
01:13:27,991 --> 01:13:29,024
What's wrong with it?
It's driving me crazy.

1519
01:13:29,324 --> 01:13:31,224
(Ace Da Bin prepares to attack.)

1520
01:13:31,524 --> 01:13:32,491
It's Da Bin!

1521
01:13:33,257 --> 01:13:36,324
(They instantly move into formation.)

1522
01:13:37,157 --> 01:13:38,124
It's Da Bin!

1523
01:13:38,124 --> 01:13:40,157
- It lands in the middle!
- It's straight.

1524
01:13:40,157 --> 01:13:42,157
(Even after reading her move,
they conceded anyway.)

1525
01:13:43,257 --> 01:13:45,357
(The pro team keeps chasing.)

1526
01:13:45,724 --> 01:13:47,257
We can catch them up.

1527
01:13:48,324 --> 01:13:50,891
The fight for every single point is
fierce.

1528
01:13:50,891 --> 01:13:52,757
(They're chasing one by one.)

1529
01:13:58,791 --> 01:14:00,391
(It's intensely neck-and-neck.)

1530
01:14:00,391 --> 01:14:02,757
Both teams continue exchanging blows.

1531
01:14:02,790 --> 01:14:05,124
Wonder Dogs need to secure their lead.

1532
01:14:05,924 --> 01:14:07,391
The gap is four points.

1533
01:14:07,391 --> 01:14:08,357
Serve!
(The team's ace, Da Bin's serve)

1534
01:14:11,791 --> 01:14:13,291
- My ball. Na Yeon.
- Seung Ju.

1535
01:14:15,557 --> 01:14:16,424
Na Yeon.

1536
01:14:16,424 --> 01:14:17,757
Myoung Hwa's sudden quick attack.

1537
01:14:17,757 --> 01:14:18,757
They defend it.

1538
01:14:18,757 --> 01:14:19,891
(Here comes Seon Ok.)

1539
01:14:21,257 --> 01:14:23,724
(When it comes to Seon Ok...)

1540
01:14:24,191 --> 01:14:27,224
(Block in between both hands)

1541
01:14:27,624 --> 01:14:29,191
(Remember, right?)

1542
01:14:29,657 --> 01:14:30,491
Hit it!

1543
01:14:31,257 --> 01:14:33,324
(It worked!)

1544
01:14:34,691 --> 01:14:37,191
A strong spike right on the spot!

1545
01:14:37,191 --> 01:14:38,633
Even Tamira!

1546
01:14:39,491 --> 01:14:42,791
(Scream for Tamira!)

1547
01:14:42,791 --> 01:14:45,391
Okay! Tamira!

1548
01:14:46,591 --> 01:14:49,091
(Proud of her)

1549
01:14:51,591 --> 01:14:54,357
Hyo Seo, was the ball supposed
to be handled like that?

1550
01:14:54,624 --> 01:14:55,691
She should have set it to the right.

1551
01:14:55,691 --> 01:14:58,691
(He chuckles his frustration away.)

1552
01:14:58,957 --> 01:15:00,557
(The match continues.)

1553
01:15:01,824 --> 01:15:03,424
(Tamira's spike)

1554
01:15:03,424 --> 01:15:05,657
- Tamira's fierce attack!
- Take it slow.

1555
01:15:06,157 --> 01:15:07,157
The ball goes high.

1556
01:15:07,157 --> 01:15:08,791
This time, Enkhsoyol is on the other side.

1557
01:15:11,024 --> 01:15:12,791
The Red Sparks save it.

1558
01:15:12,791 --> 01:15:14,191
(Here comes Seon Ok again.)

1559
01:15:14,362 --> 01:15:15,424
Consider the ball in the middle.

1560
01:15:15,424 --> 01:15:16,457
She'll jump straight up.

1561
01:15:16,457 --> 01:15:18,057
Don't let it break through. Never.

1562
01:15:18,057 --> 01:15:19,957
(Seon Ok means block
in between both hands.)

1563
01:15:20,457 --> 01:15:22,324
(Seon Ok, you're a pro volleyball player.)

1564
01:15:24,257 --> 01:15:25,591
(It worked again!)

1565
01:15:25,591 --> 01:15:26,524
She sets it.

1566
01:15:26,524 --> 01:15:28,757
(Tamira handles it perfectly again!)

1567
01:15:28,757 --> 01:15:30,624
Tamira!

1568
01:15:31,057 --> 01:15:32,591
(Tamiraculous block!)

1569
01:15:32,757 --> 01:15:34,157
Nice, Tamira!

1570
01:15:35,157 --> 01:15:37,224
Coach Kim gives a thumbs up.

1571
01:15:37,224 --> 01:15:39,424
(Tamira continues to shine
throughout the game.)

1572
01:15:39,924 --> 01:15:40,891
Tamira.

1573
01:15:41,324 --> 01:15:42,157
She saves it.

1574
01:15:43,557 --> 01:15:45,157
(Enkhsoyol is on the other side.)

1575
01:15:45,157 --> 01:15:46,924
Enkhsoyol's spike!

1576
01:15:46,924 --> 01:15:48,224
Tamira and Enkhsoyol.

1577
01:15:48,224 --> 01:15:50,357
The Mongolian Duo is dominating the court!

1578
01:15:50,791 --> 01:15:52,291
She saves it.

1579
01:15:52,624 --> 01:15:53,491
Go!

1580
01:15:54,791 --> 01:15:55,797
(Zoom.)

1581
01:15:55,924 --> 01:15:57,157
Tamira, let's go!

1582
01:15:57,158 --> 01:15:58,262
(Here comes...)

1583
01:15:58,263 --> 01:15:59,691
(Tamira!)

1584
01:16:00,824 --> 01:16:02,491
(Leap.)

1585
01:16:08,257 --> 01:16:10,991
Her tip succeeds!

1586
01:16:12,191 --> 01:16:13,791
Thank you, Tamira.

1587
01:16:14,957 --> 01:16:16,124
Yes!

1588
01:16:16,991 --> 01:16:18,224
That's good. So relief.

1589
01:16:18,687 --> 01:16:21,391
(Nice Tamira)

1590
01:16:21,391 --> 01:16:22,632
Tamira, nice.

1591
01:16:23,729 --> 01:16:24,323
(Thanks.)

1592
01:16:24,324 --> 01:16:27,691
Though Tamira's been out of the spotlight,
she's shining today.

1593
01:16:27,924 --> 01:16:30,557
(Fourth Set, Red Sparks 9
: Wonder Dogs 14)

1594
01:16:31,191 --> 01:16:34,291
(A wry laugh)

1595
01:16:35,424 --> 01:16:37,857
Seon Ok, when you block,
you need to reach out properly.

1596
01:16:37,857 --> 01:16:39,224
- Okay.
- Don't do it half-heartedly.

1597
01:16:39,224 --> 01:16:40,357
You can't do it half-heartedly.

1598
01:16:40,357 --> 01:16:41,357
No.

1599
01:16:41,357 --> 01:16:43,108
Okay. It was my mistake.

1600
01:16:43,192 --> 01:16:46,725
Enkhsoyol, watch the gap between blocks
when you're attacking.

1601
01:16:46,726 --> 01:16:48,092
(Strategy to maintain the momentum)

1602
01:16:48,174 --> 01:16:50,140
It's 14 to 9, a 5-point difference.

1603
01:16:50,707 --> 01:16:53,140
Tamira's been delivering
good serves today.

1604
01:16:54,774 --> 01:16:56,674
(Posing)

1605
01:16:59,240 --> 01:17:00,440
A strong serve.

1606
01:17:02,474 --> 01:17:03,507
From the back.

1607
01:17:03,507 --> 01:17:04,407
Slowly.

1608
01:17:04,407 --> 01:17:05,574
(Tossing to Enkhsoyol)

1609
01:17:06,174 --> 01:17:08,074
(Remember the gap)

1610
01:17:08,274 --> 01:17:09,407
(Aiming)

1611
01:17:13,107 --> 01:17:15,564
Enkhsoyol. Yes!

1612
01:17:15,589 --> 01:17:16,949
(It worked again!)

1613
01:17:16,974 --> 01:17:19,040
That's a point for the Mongolian duo.

1614
01:17:19,040 --> 01:17:20,640
(A forward-thinking tactic)

1615
01:17:21,040 --> 01:17:22,107
Tamira, nice serve!

1616
01:17:23,474 --> 01:17:25,174
Tamira in the back...

1617
01:17:25,174 --> 01:17:27,207
and Enkhsoyol in the front.

1618
01:17:27,207 --> 01:17:29,040
- We always score a lot with this combo.
- We do.

1619
01:17:29,440 --> 01:17:32,574
When are we supposed to hit it straight?

1620
01:17:32,574 --> 01:17:33,407
When it's high.

1621
01:17:33,407 --> 01:17:38,507
You start in Zone 1, and when it's up
in Zone 4, you go to your position.

1622
01:17:39,740 --> 01:17:43,974
(Whenever they had time during training,)

1623
01:17:44,840 --> 01:17:51,740
(the Mongolian duo talked about volleyball
and coordinated.)

1624
01:17:52,474 --> 01:17:55,407
The strong serves from Tamira
create opportunities,

1625
01:17:55,407 --> 01:17:58,040
and Enkhsoyol turns that
into scoring moments.

1626
01:17:58,972 --> 01:18:02,974
Actually, Tamira and Enkhsoyol speak
very good Korean.

1627
01:18:02,974 --> 01:18:03,940
However,

1628
01:18:03,940 --> 01:18:06,248
they sometimes pretend
they don't understand.

1629
01:18:06,974 --> 01:18:09,807
- Today, they understood.
- Yes, everything.

1630
01:18:09,974 --> 01:18:12,540
(Wonder Dogs riding the momentum)

1631
01:18:13,507 --> 01:18:16,040
(Tamira's serve again)

1632
01:18:19,474 --> 01:18:20,607
Da Bin receives it.

1633
01:18:21,240 --> 01:18:22,107
Hit it!

1634
01:18:23,466 --> 01:18:25,966
Seon Ok hits a lot of diagonals.

1635
01:18:27,174 --> 01:18:29,374
(Moving to diagonal position)

1636
01:18:32,274 --> 01:18:33,407
It's in.

1637
01:18:33,907 --> 01:18:36,007
(She didn't hit it diagonally.)

1638
01:18:36,607 --> 01:18:37,874
That was a good move.

1639
01:18:37,874 --> 01:18:39,740
Na Yeon, it was my fault. Sorry.

1640
01:18:40,674 --> 01:18:43,207
(All Seon Ok's diagonal attacks were...)

1641
01:18:43,674 --> 01:18:46,140
(blocked by Wonder Dogs so far.)

1642
01:18:48,340 --> 01:18:49,974
(Spotting an empty spot)

1643
01:18:50,674 --> 01:18:52,074
She twisted and hit it straight.

1644
01:18:52,074 --> 01:18:53,440
Seon Ok won a point.

1645
01:18:53,907 --> 01:18:56,074
It was the defense's fault. Sorry.

1646
01:18:56,907 --> 01:18:58,340
Let's just do one point.

1647
01:19:00,274 --> 01:19:02,874
(Seon Ok's serve)

1648
01:19:04,307 --> 01:19:05,240
Seung Ju.

1649
01:19:05,740 --> 01:19:06,640
Na Yeon.

1650
01:19:08,407 --> 01:19:09,507
Enkhsoyol!

1651
01:19:09,840 --> 01:19:10,807
They blocked it.

1652
01:19:11,640 --> 01:19:13,040
A free ball for Wonder Dogs.

1653
01:19:13,907 --> 01:19:14,774
They set it.

1654
01:19:14,774 --> 01:19:16,374
(A free ball)

1655
01:19:16,374 --> 01:19:17,974
(It's an opportunity!)

1656
01:19:21,040 --> 01:19:23,607
A slide attack! But it's blocked.

1657
01:19:23,607 --> 01:19:26,274
Da Bin delivers a solo block!

1658
01:19:26,274 --> 01:19:27,574
- Nice catch.
- Nice catch.

1659
01:19:27,574 --> 01:19:30,007
(Red Sparks building their momentum)

1660
01:19:33,174 --> 01:19:35,540
(They can't let them take control.)

1661
01:19:35,540 --> 01:19:37,274
Let's just do one.

1662
01:19:38,040 --> 01:19:39,574
Stay focused!

1663
01:19:39,574 --> 01:19:41,874
(Fourth set, Red Sparks 11
: Wonder Dogs 15)

1664
01:19:42,307 --> 01:19:45,107
(Again, Seon Ok's serve)

1665
01:19:48,940 --> 01:19:49,807
Enkhsoyol.

1666
01:19:50,440 --> 01:19:51,674
The reception was a bit shaky.

1667
01:19:54,407 --> 01:19:55,574
A rebound play.

1668
01:19:56,807 --> 01:19:57,974
(The ball gets tossed over.)

1669
01:19:57,974 --> 01:19:59,328
Is the ball going over the net?

1670
01:19:59,507 --> 01:20:01,540
(Spotting a perfect chance)

1671
01:20:01,774 --> 01:20:04,124
This team has a unique characteristic.

1672
01:20:04,148 --> 01:20:06,507
They once came back from 19 to 24...

1673
01:20:06,507 --> 01:20:08,474
and won the set.

1674
01:20:08,474 --> 01:20:10,007
They're like zombies.

1675
01:20:11,174 --> 01:20:12,837
It was empty.

1676
01:20:12,875 --> 01:20:14,149
Let's keep it up!

1677
01:20:14,174 --> 01:20:17,207
Ace player Jung Da Bin is
scoring consecutively.

1678
01:20:18,240 --> 01:20:19,940
What is wrong with them?

1679
01:20:19,940 --> 01:20:20,807
Da Bin!

1680
01:20:21,207 --> 01:20:22,174
Nice one.

1681
01:20:22,174 --> 01:20:23,574
(Now that they're on a roll,)

1682
01:20:24,140 --> 01:20:25,074
(they're coming back like zombies.)

1683
01:20:25,074 --> 01:20:26,440
Down to a three-point difference.

1684
01:20:26,440 --> 01:20:28,574
The Red Sparks are
tenaciously catching up!

1685
01:20:28,574 --> 01:20:29,807
(Deep in thought)

1686
01:20:30,040 --> 01:20:30,874
Tamira.

1687
01:20:32,907 --> 01:20:35,674
She's pulling out Tamira
and subbing in Su Bin.

1688
01:20:36,940 --> 01:20:40,007
Sol is back on the court as well.

1689
01:20:41,440 --> 01:20:44,707
Now, Su Bin will be defending
from the back.

1690
01:20:44,707 --> 01:20:47,207
- They need to get in form quickly.
- Yes.

1691
01:20:47,807 --> 01:20:49,007
Hyo Seo receives.

1692
01:20:49,316 --> 01:20:50,915
- Hit it!
- Hit it!

1693
01:20:50,940 --> 01:20:52,340
(Da Bin never gets tired of attacking.)

1694
01:20:52,340 --> 01:20:54,107
Da Bin. They receive the ball!

1695
01:20:54,107 --> 01:20:55,574
(The ball was a hand touch.)

1696
01:20:57,007 --> 01:20:58,540
Seung Ju is rushing over!

1697
01:20:58,540 --> 01:20:59,440
Get it!

1698
01:21:04,240 --> 01:21:06,107
She's rushing over!

1699
01:21:06,107 --> 01:21:06,907
Be careful.

1700
01:21:06,907 --> 01:21:08,407
(Touch out)

1701
01:21:08,840 --> 01:21:10,840
(Fourth set, Red Sparks 13
: Wonder Dogs 16)

1702
01:21:10,840 --> 01:21:12,607
Seung Ju threw herself at the ball.

1703
01:21:13,240 --> 01:21:17,207
That's how desperate
the players are for victory.

1704
01:21:18,674 --> 01:21:20,807
(The fourth set will decide
the team's existence.)

1705
01:21:22,174 --> 01:21:25,307
(Playing against yesterday's teammates)

1706
01:21:25,874 --> 01:21:27,740
Hey, we have to go right away!

1707
01:21:27,740 --> 01:21:30,140
We're only one set away from disbandment.

1708
01:21:30,907 --> 01:21:34,140
I'm not the same person I was before.

1709
01:21:35,440 --> 01:21:36,640
It's not about whether we can win.

1710
01:21:36,640 --> 01:21:39,740
I believe that we absolutely have to win.

1711
01:21:39,765 --> 01:21:41,209
(Win at all costs!)

1712
01:21:47,340 --> 01:21:49,674
(Ye Rim's serve)

1713
01:21:52,261 --> 01:21:53,041
Get it!

1714
01:21:53,574 --> 01:21:54,540
The ball drops.

1715
01:21:55,510 --> 01:21:57,574
(Chasing with full energy...)

1716
01:21:58,007 --> 01:21:59,807
(and tossing it to Seung Ju)

1717
01:22:00,440 --> 01:22:02,574
(But the opponent formed blocks
right away.)

1718
01:22:03,007 --> 01:22:05,407
(Another defense
in the diagonal direction)

1719
01:22:05,607 --> 01:22:08,007
(Every angle is blocked.)

1720
01:22:08,674 --> 01:22:09,874
Get it.

1721
01:22:09,874 --> 01:22:12,874
I think real volleyball is...

1722
01:22:12,874 --> 01:22:15,074
about a call from the setter,

1723
01:22:15,074 --> 01:22:17,140
or a call from the attacker.

1724
01:22:17,674 --> 01:22:22,874
I believe that a small difference can
decide the match's outcome.

1725
01:22:23,940 --> 01:22:26,774
(And Seung Ju made a call.)

1726
01:22:27,440 --> 01:22:29,307
Seung Ju spikes and scores!

1727
01:22:29,840 --> 01:22:30,907
That's it!

1728
01:22:32,507 --> 01:22:34,340
A touch-out point off the blocker.

1729
01:22:35,540 --> 01:22:38,574
Seung Ju is providing answers for herself.

1730
01:22:39,874 --> 01:22:41,674
(She checked the defense
in the diagonal direction.)

1731
01:22:42,640 --> 01:22:44,126
You have to hit it out
in these circumstances.

1732
01:22:45,240 --> 01:22:46,507
She won a point.

1733
01:22:48,307 --> 01:22:49,974
Oh, man. That was close.

1734
01:22:49,974 --> 01:22:52,640
(Seung Ju finally stopped
the opponent's winning streak.)

1735
01:22:59,707 --> 01:23:01,274
A faint tip. It gets blocked.

1736
01:23:02,940 --> 01:23:03,807
Spike!

1737
01:23:03,807 --> 01:23:04,940
They defend it!

1738
01:23:05,340 --> 01:23:07,074
Stay calm and set it up high.

1739
01:23:08,107 --> 01:23:09,474
Seung Ju tips over at the net.

1740
01:23:10,640 --> 01:23:11,574
Go!

1741
01:23:12,174 --> 01:23:13,374
Da Bin's spike.

1742
01:23:13,374 --> 01:23:15,074
Setting it up in the back.

1743
01:23:15,074 --> 01:23:16,074
Jump!

1744
01:23:18,140 --> 01:23:20,074
Seung Ju spikes!

1745
01:23:20,074 --> 01:23:22,307
- She scores!
- Nice attack!

1746
01:23:22,307 --> 01:23:23,907
It was a great angle.

1747
01:23:24,307 --> 01:23:27,774
Dr. Pyo is leading the game,
giving it her all.

1748
01:23:27,774 --> 01:23:28,907
We're doing great. Just one more.

1749
01:23:28,907 --> 01:23:30,240
Back to a four-point difference.

1750
01:23:30,240 --> 01:23:32,007
Wonder Dogs widen the gap.

1751
01:23:33,040 --> 01:23:35,207
(The momentum is back with Wonder Dogs.)

1752
01:23:36,607 --> 01:23:37,740
Da Bin serving.

1753
01:23:39,140 --> 01:23:40,040
Mine.

1754
01:23:41,640 --> 01:23:43,374
- Seung Ju.
- Hit it.

1755
01:23:44,907 --> 01:23:46,340
(Tamira's spike)

1756
01:23:46,340 --> 01:23:48,040
Spike from the right!

1757
01:23:48,040 --> 01:23:50,340
- Tamira!
- Let's push it, guys.

1758
01:23:51,474 --> 01:23:54,574
Red Sparks players couldn't get
into defensive positions in time,

1759
01:23:54,574 --> 01:23:57,140
so they were running back and forth.

1760
01:23:57,140 --> 01:23:59,474
- It's not easy to block.
- Absolutely not.

1761
01:24:00,707 --> 01:24:03,140
(Captain Pyo serving, riding the momentum)

1762
01:24:03,640 --> 01:24:04,907
(Glancing)

1763
01:24:05,640 --> 01:24:07,540
(Target serve to Zone 3)

1764
01:24:07,807 --> 01:24:09,040
(Message received)

1765
01:24:10,207 --> 01:24:11,274
One, two, three.

1766
01:24:11,274 --> 01:24:12,307
Nice serve!

1767
01:24:12,307 --> 01:24:13,540
(Target serve to Zone 3)

1768
01:24:13,540 --> 01:24:15,240
(And that's where she served!)

1769
01:24:16,074 --> 01:24:19,140
(Is the middle blocker
attempting to attack?)

1770
01:24:19,874 --> 01:24:22,807
(Fine. I'll block it.)

1771
01:24:23,240 --> 01:24:24,140
Hit it!

1772
01:24:25,340 --> 01:24:27,540
(Successful solo block)

1773
01:24:27,540 --> 01:24:30,540
Spiking in the middle, and it's blocked!

1774
01:24:30,540 --> 01:24:33,574
A decisive block by Myoung Hwa!

1775
01:24:33,574 --> 01:24:36,440
We don't have another middle blocker
for substitution today.

1776
01:24:36,440 --> 01:24:38,207
But she's doing such a wonderful job.

1777
01:24:38,207 --> 01:24:40,774
(Fourth set, Red Sparks 16
: Wonder Dogs 21)

1778
01:24:41,774 --> 01:24:42,974
(The game continues.)

1779
01:24:42,974 --> 01:24:43,874
Hye In.

1780
01:24:44,574 --> 01:24:45,440
Sol.

1781
01:24:46,674 --> 01:24:48,240
Enkhsoyol!

1782
01:24:48,240 --> 01:24:49,340
So clean and precise!

1783
01:24:51,107 --> 01:24:54,040
(Fourth set, Red Sparks 18
: Wonder Dogs 22)

1784
01:24:56,507 --> 01:24:57,574
It was a mistake.

1785
01:24:59,507 --> 01:25:00,540
Eun Ji serving.

1786
01:25:01,874 --> 01:25:04,274
We need points, guys.

1787
01:25:04,274 --> 01:25:05,240
(Ready to receive, turning to the side)

1788
01:25:08,274 --> 01:25:09,340
Enkhsoyol receives.

1789
01:25:12,074 --> 01:25:13,007
Enkhsoyol!

1790
01:25:13,574 --> 01:25:15,007
It's out!

1791
01:25:16,207 --> 01:25:18,807
It was a touch-out!

1792
01:25:20,074 --> 01:25:20,940
No touch.

1793
01:25:21,307 --> 01:25:22,240
No.

1794
01:25:24,107 --> 01:25:25,807
They're requesting a video review.

1795
01:25:27,907 --> 01:25:30,240
(Finger shaking)

1796
01:25:31,074 --> 01:25:33,940
- Seo Hyun's finger was shaking.
- Her middle finger.

1797
01:25:35,207 --> 01:25:37,340
- It was touched.
- It's a touch-out.

1798
01:25:37,340 --> 01:25:38,774
It touched her finger.

1799
01:25:38,774 --> 01:25:40,440
Stay more focused, guys.

1800
01:25:44,374 --> 01:25:45,774
She hits it well on the rise.

1801
01:25:48,140 --> 01:25:50,007
- Nice serve!
- Tamira serving.

1802
01:25:51,940 --> 01:25:53,107
(Spicy service coming)

1803
01:25:53,107 --> 01:25:53,974
Push it.

1804
01:25:54,207 --> 01:25:55,040
Seo Hyun.

1805
01:25:55,507 --> 01:25:56,374
Quick attack.

1806
01:25:56,374 --> 01:25:58,374
(Is it breaking through their defense?)

1807
01:25:58,507 --> 01:26:00,040
It's a tip!

1808
01:26:05,474 --> 01:26:07,774
Hye In dives and saves it!

1809
01:26:09,374 --> 01:26:11,674
(They hit it in a rush...)

1810
01:26:11,674 --> 01:26:12,940
It's out!

1811
01:26:12,940 --> 01:26:15,507
- It's a block out.
- An unforced error!

1812
01:26:16,407 --> 01:26:17,274
Is it out?

1813
01:26:18,407 --> 01:26:19,274
Sorry.

1814
01:26:23,274 --> 01:26:26,174
(Only one point to win the game)

1815
01:26:26,474 --> 01:26:27,807
Nice defense, Hye In.

1816
01:26:27,807 --> 01:26:29,407
- That was a nice set.
- Okay.

1817
01:26:30,340 --> 01:26:32,740
They're really in sync, and it's showing.

1818
01:26:32,740 --> 01:26:33,574
Absolutely.

1819
01:26:33,574 --> 01:26:37,040
Wonder Dogs are becoming one,
just like that!

1820
01:26:37,040 --> 01:26:40,874
A good dig caused the opponent's error.

1821
01:26:40,874 --> 01:26:45,033
Pilseung Wonder Dogs' match point
for today's game!

1822
01:26:45,052 --> 01:26:46,339
(Fourth set, Red Sparks 19
: Wonder Dogs 24)

1823
01:26:46,783 --> 01:26:48,952
- Just one more clean point.
- Yes.

1824
01:26:51,488 --> 01:26:53,290
They have to seal the deal right here!

1825
01:26:54,224 --> 01:26:56,993
(About a month ago,
during Wonder Dogs' second match,)

1826
01:27:00,864 --> 01:27:04,901
(they suffered a narrow defeat
to a pro team.)

1827
01:27:06,503 --> 01:27:11,908
(A bitter pain they vowed never
to feel again)

1828
01:27:13,476 --> 01:27:17,113
(Now, their chance
for redemption has arrived.)

1829
01:27:17,781 --> 01:27:20,123
Hyeon Jeong, watch out for a short serve.

1830
01:27:20,147 --> 01:27:21,603
It will be on the left side.

1831
01:27:22,685 --> 01:27:25,421
(Seon Ok's serve)

1832
01:27:27,657 --> 01:27:28,491
Mine.

1833
01:27:29,125 --> 01:27:30,093
Mine.

1834
01:27:30,093 --> 01:27:33,196
(Pyo Seung Ju, outside hitter,
retired from Red Sparks in 2025)

1835
01:27:35,698 --> 01:27:38,701
(Koo Sol, striker,
removed from Red Sparks in 2020)

1836
01:27:38,701 --> 01:27:39,669
- Mine.
- You have to go!

1837
01:27:39,669 --> 01:27:40,722
- Seung Ju.
- Go for it.

1838
01:27:41,137 --> 01:27:41,938
Sol.

1839
01:27:41,938 --> 01:27:43,673
(The hangs in the air.)

1840
01:27:44,207 --> 01:27:48,311
(And teammates are right behind you,
watching your back)

1841
01:27:49,079 --> 01:27:51,548
(Let's do it!)

1842
01:27:52,382 --> 01:27:54,117
(From underdogs...)

1843
01:27:54,117 --> 01:27:56,219
(to Wonder Dogs)

1844
01:27:57,754 --> 01:27:58,588
Mine.

1845
01:27:58,788 --> 01:28:00,041
- Seung Ju.
- You should go.

1846
01:28:00,190 --> 01:28:00,991
Sol.

1847
01:28:01,210 --> 01:28:05,581
- Enkhsoyol, spike!
- Nice!

1848
01:28:09,265 --> 01:28:10,399
We won!

1849
01:28:10,900 --> 01:28:12,602
- Enkhsoyol, spike!
- Nice!

1850
01:28:12,602 --> 01:28:16,973
(Enkhsoyol's final blow)

1851
01:28:19,776 --> 01:28:24,180
(Fourth set, Red Sparks 19
: Wonder Dogs 25)

1852
01:28:27,117 --> 01:28:29,152
(Exclaiming)

1853
01:28:30,286 --> 01:28:34,123
(Shouting in excitement)

1854
01:28:35,492 --> 01:28:36,893
What just happened?

1855
01:28:36,893 --> 01:28:40,129
Against Red Sparks, Wonder Dogs have...

1856
01:28:40,129 --> 01:28:43,399
secured a victory
with a set score of 3 to 1!

1857
01:28:43,399 --> 01:28:44,533
(Wonder Dogs win.)

1858
01:28:44,534 --> 01:28:46,703
This is the third consecutive victory
of Wonder Dogs,

1859
01:28:46,703 --> 01:28:48,805
- and they have ensured their survival!
- They ensured their survival.

1860
01:28:52,308 --> 01:28:53,943
We beat Red Sparks.

1861
01:28:54,152 --> 01:28:55,120
(Clapping)

1862
01:28:55,145 --> 01:28:58,448
- You don't look very happy.
- Yes, I am! I'm extremely happy.

1863
01:28:59,282 --> 01:29:00,816
Thank you. Good job today.

1864
01:29:02,178 --> 01:29:03,328
(Empty laugh)

1865
01:29:03,353 --> 01:29:04,721
Why are you laughing?

1866
01:29:11,995 --> 01:29:14,164
Red Sparks' coach is mad,
but he still smiled at me.

1867
01:29:15,832 --> 01:29:17,533
- Thank you for your work.
- Good job.

1868
01:29:17,533 --> 01:29:20,136
- Great game.
- Thank you.

1869
01:29:20,403 --> 01:29:21,804
(Rushing)

1870
01:29:22,305 --> 01:29:24,340
(Captain Pyo is the most excited.)

1871
01:29:25,708 --> 01:29:28,311
(Smiling brightly)

1872
01:29:28,678 --> 01:29:30,413
Nice job.

1873
01:29:30,413 --> 01:29:33,983
(Sharing the joy of victory
to the fullest)

1874
01:29:35,084 --> 01:29:37,219
Wonder Dogs, good job securing the game.

1875
01:29:37,287 --> 01:29:39,756
Now, we won't be disbanded.

1876
01:29:40,657 --> 01:29:42,959
I felt so happy and relieved,
realizing we had won.

1877
01:29:43,626 --> 01:29:46,462
I was very happy today,

1878
01:29:46,462 --> 01:29:50,333
since it was my first time playing
on the court for so long.

1879
01:29:50,333 --> 01:29:52,235
And I'm very happy we won.

1880
01:29:53,236 --> 01:29:55,471
To be honest,
as soon as we won the match today,

1881
01:29:55,471 --> 01:29:57,440
I was very happy,

1882
01:29:57,440 --> 01:29:58,841
but the first thing I felt was relief,

1883
01:29:58,841 --> 01:30:00,943
knowing we wouldn't be disbanded.

1884
01:30:00,943 --> 01:30:02,945
I always felt...

1885
01:30:02,945 --> 01:30:04,814
like we had something to prove.

1886
01:30:04,814 --> 01:30:07,817
And I'm very glad
that we actually managed to do it.

1887
01:30:08,551 --> 01:30:10,987
Surely, I'm very happy.

1888
01:30:11,521 --> 01:30:13,957
In the end,
there's always a way to survive.

1889
01:30:14,390 --> 01:30:16,325
When you win a match,

1890
01:30:16,326 --> 01:30:19,629
you certainly feel the thrill
and a sense of fulfillment.

1891
01:30:19,896 --> 01:30:21,798
So, I'm proud of my team...

1892
01:30:22,131 --> 01:30:23,732
and I feel thankful toward my players.

1893
01:30:23,733 --> 01:30:26,202
It gives me some optimistic thoughts
about what's ahead.

1894
01:30:27,970 --> 01:30:29,872
(Afterward)

1895
01:30:30,506 --> 01:30:32,842
(Seung Ju walks to someone.)

1896
01:30:32,842 --> 01:30:33,978
- You've trained hard.
- Yes?

1897
01:30:33,978 --> 01:30:35,078
You've trained quite a lot.

1898
01:30:35,245 --> 01:30:37,847
- I'm working out a lot.
- I can see that.

1899
01:30:37,847 --> 01:30:39,182
- I recognized it.
- What?

1900
01:30:39,182 --> 01:30:40,583
Your knees look good too.

1901
01:30:41,451 --> 01:30:42,352
You're good.

1902
01:30:43,853 --> 01:30:44,887
How are you doing?

1903
01:30:45,355 --> 01:30:46,256
I'm good.

1904
01:30:47,890 --> 01:30:49,892
I knew you'd play well.

1905
01:30:49,892 --> 01:30:51,260
What? No.

1906
01:30:51,260 --> 01:30:52,061
As I thought,

1907
01:30:52,929 --> 01:30:54,230
you're a good volleyball player.

1908
01:30:56,332 --> 01:30:58,534
Keep going and stay in touch.

1909
01:30:58,534 --> 01:30:59,668
- Okay.
- All right?

1910
01:31:00,770 --> 01:31:04,540
Do you mind if I come
to see your matches next time?

1911
01:31:04,540 --> 01:31:05,860
Not at all. You definitely should.

1912
01:31:06,175 --> 01:31:08,477
I was careful with contacting you.

1913
01:31:08,478 --> 01:31:09,946
- Why that?
- Because...

1914
01:31:09,946 --> 01:31:13,183
I wanted to talk to you in person first.

1915
01:31:13,683 --> 01:31:15,652
Just feel free to come and contact me
whenever you want.

1916
01:31:15,885 --> 01:31:16,786
Okay?

1917
01:31:17,654 --> 01:31:19,155
Yes, sir.

1918
01:31:21,524 --> 01:31:22,944
I have mixed emotions.

1919
01:31:23,793 --> 01:31:25,461
You know, it's...

1920
01:31:26,696 --> 01:31:28,998
Even though you want
to keep the players for a bit longer,

1921
01:31:30,433 --> 01:31:34,404
you have to dismiss them
due to the team's circumstances.

1922
01:31:34,570 --> 01:31:39,575
It's quite tough. Yes.

1923
01:31:40,677 --> 01:31:42,712
She'll do well.

1924
01:31:42,712 --> 01:31:45,281
Because she's a great player.

1925
01:31:46,182 --> 01:31:47,517
She always has been.

1926
01:31:51,321 --> 01:31:55,091
I really had mixed emotions.

1927
01:31:55,258 --> 01:31:58,862
It felt very strange.

1928
01:32:00,463 --> 01:32:01,664
Good job, guys.

1929
01:32:02,284 --> 01:32:04,720
In the end, they're my old teammates.

1930
01:32:05,268 --> 01:32:07,503
Only a few months ago,

1931
01:32:07,503 --> 01:32:09,972
I used to be a part of them.

1932
01:32:10,907 --> 01:32:17,546
So, watching them lose the game
made me feel sorry for them.

1933
01:32:17,547 --> 01:32:18,481
It's okay.

1934
01:32:18,481 --> 01:32:19,582
(She felt sorry for them.)

1935
01:32:21,117 --> 01:32:24,320
(She could have been playing
on their side of the court today.)

1936
01:32:24,620 --> 01:32:28,190
I'm glad our final memory was a good one.

1937
01:32:28,991 --> 01:32:32,561
But above all things,
the fact that we won today...

1938
01:32:32,695 --> 01:32:33,963
makes me most happy.

1939
01:32:34,130 --> 01:32:35,131
No.

1940
01:32:37,066 --> 01:32:38,834
We won't be disbanded!

1941
01:32:39,435 --> 01:32:41,370
No disbandment!

1942
01:32:41,604 --> 01:32:43,706
We saved ourselves!

1943
01:32:45,575 --> 01:32:47,677
(Wonder Dogs saved their lives.)

1944
01:32:47,677 --> 01:32:50,079
Is this ours now?
Tell them to bring them back quickly.

1945
01:32:51,214 --> 01:32:53,115
Let's ask them to reassemble
all of the other parts.

1946
01:32:53,115 --> 01:32:54,883
Couldn't we just reassemble all parts?

1947
01:32:55,118 --> 01:32:57,153
The important thing is
that we won't be disbanded.

1948
01:32:57,153 --> 01:32:59,489
Let's hold it like this
after our final game.

1949
01:32:59,648 --> 01:33:00,623
We should raise it like this.

1950
01:33:00,623 --> 01:33:01,824
(Everyone is smiling widely
after securing their survival.)

1951
01:33:03,926 --> 01:33:07,696
(The locker room was once filled
with silence and sighs.)

1952
01:33:08,364 --> 01:33:10,399
No, stop now.

1953
01:33:10,399 --> 01:33:11,967
(Today, we'll laugh as much as we like!)

1954
01:33:13,637 --> 01:33:15,371
Congratulations on your victory.

1955
01:33:18,441 --> 01:33:22,011
As of today,
the record is 4 wins and 2 losses.

1956
01:33:22,779 --> 01:33:24,180
You've survived.

1957
01:33:28,985 --> 01:33:31,321
We'll announce your next opponent.

1958
01:33:32,422 --> 01:33:34,124
(An intense 50-day journey
without any break)

1959
01:33:34,957 --> 01:33:37,126
(In the long-awaited first match,)

1960
01:33:38,294 --> 01:33:41,197
(they secured their first victory
against Geunyoung Girls' High...)

1961
01:33:41,697 --> 01:33:45,334
(and spectacularly kicked off the show.)

1962
01:33:45,735 --> 01:33:47,437
(However)

1963
01:33:47,537 --> 01:33:49,038
(Altos, a professional team)

1964
01:33:49,038 --> 01:33:50,306
(Defeat)

1965
01:33:50,706 --> 01:33:52,441
(Shujitsu High School,
the Japanese female high school champion)

1966
01:33:52,441 --> 01:33:55,044
(Defeat)

1967
01:33:55,411 --> 01:33:58,614
(With two consecutive defeats,
their winning rate was 33 percent.)

1968
01:33:58,614 --> 01:34:01,317
(And they were on the brink
of disbandment.)

1969
01:34:02,185 --> 01:34:03,085
(We must...)

1970
01:34:03,085 --> 01:34:05,220
(become stronger!)

1971
01:34:05,922 --> 01:34:08,758
(With all their desperation)

1972
01:34:08,758 --> 01:34:10,460
(Kwangju Women's University,
the university league champion)

1973
01:34:10,726 --> 01:34:12,361
(Suwon Special City,
the corporate league champion)

1974
01:34:12,528 --> 01:34:14,363
(The Red Sparks,
the professional league runner-up)

1975
01:34:14,363 --> 01:34:16,799
(They beat all three of them in a row,
achieving a three-consecutive win.)

1976
01:34:17,233 --> 01:34:18,868
(With a score of 4 wins and 2 losses,)

1977
01:34:18,868 --> 01:34:20,503
(Wonder Dogs have secured their survival.)

1978
01:34:20,837 --> 01:34:22,839
(And finally,)

1979
01:34:23,239 --> 01:34:25,174
(the final opponent)

1980
01:34:26,609 --> 01:34:27,977
(First place in V-League
and V-League Finals from 2005 to 2009)

1981
01:34:27,977 --> 01:34:29,312
(First place in V-League from 2016 to 2019
and first place in 2019 V-League Finals)

1982
01:34:29,312 --> 01:34:30,413
(First place in 2023 V-League
and first place in 2025 V-League Finals)

1983
01:34:30,913 --> 01:34:33,582
(The winningest team in V-League)

1984
01:34:34,484 --> 01:34:36,953
(The V-League champion from 2024 to 2025)

1985
01:34:47,363 --> 01:34:49,732
(From debut)

1986
01:34:50,433 --> 01:34:53,236
(To retirement)

1987
01:34:53,502 --> 01:34:55,871
(A 20-year-long companionship)

1988
01:34:56,439 --> 01:34:58,908
(Yeon Koung and Pink Spiders)

1989
01:35:00,142 --> 01:35:04,613
(They're almost like family.)

1990
01:35:07,083 --> 01:35:10,386
(For the past 20 years,
player Yeon Koung has cultivated...)

1991
01:35:11,153 --> 01:35:16,125
(their championship
in the 2025 professional league.)

1992
01:35:16,892 --> 01:35:20,095
(Against the title she had earned
herself as a player,)

1993
01:35:21,330 --> 01:35:25,067
(she now takes on the challenge
as a coach.)

1994
01:35:29,438 --> 01:35:32,341
As you already know,
our next match will be open to the public.

1995
01:35:34,443 --> 01:35:35,744
(During the shooting,
we've invited spectators through SNS.)

1996
01:35:35,745 --> 01:35:38,915
(We invite you to our match.
Please cheer for Wonder Dogs on-site!)

1997
01:35:38,981 --> 01:35:39,915
Within three days,

1998
01:35:40,316 --> 01:35:42,518
(almost ten thousand people applied.)

1999
01:35:43,586 --> 01:35:45,087
Our final match will be...

2000
01:35:45,755 --> 01:35:49,659
spectated by lots of volleyball fans
and viewers.

2001
01:35:49,659 --> 01:35:50,960
(An opportunity to prove their skills)

2002
01:35:51,260 --> 01:35:52,428
(Inside a stadium full of spectators,)

2003
01:35:52,428 --> 01:35:54,497
We've got so much to show.

2004
01:35:55,064 --> 01:35:58,100
(They'll find their initial resolve
once again.)

2005
01:35:58,467 --> 01:36:01,971
(During the tryout on July 12, 2025)

2006
01:36:02,305 --> 01:36:05,408
(Their journey began
solely with desperation)

2007
01:36:06,308 --> 01:36:07,943
If not now,

2008
01:36:07,943 --> 01:36:09,597
there won't be another chance.

2009
01:36:09,879 --> 01:36:12,615
It was just desperation.

2010
01:36:15,151 --> 01:36:18,755
(The final show)

2011
01:36:19,221 --> 01:36:22,191
(To prove themselves)

2012
01:36:29,065 --> 01:36:30,567
I'm not going easy on them at all.

2013
01:36:30,900 --> 01:36:34,103
I'll prepare winning strategies
and secure our victory, no matter what.

2014
01:36:35,304 --> 01:36:36,705
Whether it's training or the actual match,

2015
01:36:36,772 --> 01:36:39,241
I want to give it my all,
so I will leave no regrets.

2016
01:36:39,842 --> 01:36:41,629
Since it's our last game,

2017
01:36:41,653 --> 01:36:43,353
I really want to win.

2018
01:36:49,186 --> 01:36:53,686
We talked about what you did well
and what you could improve on.

2019
01:36:54,020 --> 01:36:55,853
Throughout six matches,

2020
01:36:55,853 --> 01:36:59,920
we never took the lead
at the start of the game.

2021
01:37:00,520 --> 01:37:04,720
We always began the first set
by losing four to six points.

2022
01:37:04,720 --> 01:37:09,086
In the match against the Red Sparks,
we made a new record of nine to zero.

2023
01:37:09,086 --> 01:37:12,520
We're always weak at the start.

2024
01:37:12,520 --> 01:37:15,520
When we begin, we go like "Oh, man."

2025
01:37:16,686 --> 01:37:17,920
"Oh, no."

2026
01:37:18,686 --> 01:37:20,253
"Gosh."

2027
01:37:23,120 --> 01:37:24,520
You said "Oh" nine times...

2028
01:37:24,520 --> 01:37:26,020
and the score became nine to zero.

2029
01:37:28,386 --> 01:37:30,220
You made the game harder...

2030
01:37:30,520 --> 01:37:32,453
which could have been won three to zero.

2031
01:37:32,986 --> 01:37:34,986
What do you think is the reason, Sol?

2032
01:37:38,320 --> 01:37:39,320
Nothing?

2033
01:37:40,853 --> 01:37:42,020
Are you meditating?

2034
01:37:42,820 --> 01:37:44,353
I don't know.

2035
01:37:44,353 --> 01:37:47,286
It's your match. How come you don't know?

2036
01:37:47,686 --> 01:37:48,686
What about you, Myoung Hwa?

2037
01:37:49,020 --> 01:37:54,353
For me, I'm a bit slow
to focus on the game.

2038
01:37:54,353 --> 01:37:55,886
Why are you slow then?

2039
01:37:56,386 --> 01:37:58,620
I know. It's making me crazy.

2040
01:37:59,286 --> 01:38:01,586
- Why are you slow?
- It makes me mad.

2041
01:38:01,586 --> 01:38:03,686
(The overwhelmed slow starter)

2042
01:38:03,686 --> 01:38:06,753
So we prepared a video for you.

2043
01:38:07,086 --> 01:38:09,053
Watch. It's eight to zero.

2044
01:38:09,520 --> 01:38:11,753
(The first set against the Red Sparks
with the score of 8 to 0)

2045
01:38:12,286 --> 01:38:14,186
(Tipping and tipping)

2046
01:38:14,186 --> 01:38:15,186
You tip again.

2047
01:38:16,253 --> 01:38:17,453
(Tipping once more)

2048
01:38:17,453 --> 01:38:18,453
Another tip.

2049
01:38:18,686 --> 01:38:20,986
It's eight to zero, right?

2050
01:38:20,986 --> 01:38:24,053
Don't you think
you should take some risks?

2051
01:38:24,053 --> 01:38:25,886
But none of you is doing that.

2052
01:38:25,886 --> 01:38:26,986
You all just tip.

2053
01:38:26,986 --> 01:38:28,920
Were you getting a point with tips?

2054
01:38:28,920 --> 01:38:30,953
- No.
- You should hit hard!

2055
01:38:30,953 --> 01:38:33,453
Hitters must make the decision.

2056
01:38:33,786 --> 01:38:36,153
But for our last match,

2057
01:38:36,653 --> 01:38:39,520
we'll get the upper hand
at the start of the game.

2058
01:38:39,520 --> 01:38:41,853
And then plan how we'll play the game.

2059
01:38:41,853 --> 01:38:43,353
When we come up with the plan,

2060
01:38:43,353 --> 01:38:47,453
you must follow around 98 percent of it.

2061
01:38:47,453 --> 01:38:48,453
It's not hard to do.

2062
01:38:48,453 --> 01:38:49,820
For example, you're about to attack.

2063
01:38:49,820 --> 01:38:53,686
When you have to toss the ball up
and the hitter raises her hand,

2064
01:38:53,686 --> 01:38:56,853
set it up in front of her right eye.

2065
01:38:56,853 --> 01:39:02,686
I'm not asking you to do
impossible things like that.

2066
01:39:02,686 --> 01:39:06,086
We plan for our game
like what we're doing now.

2067
01:39:06,086 --> 01:39:08,286
What do you have to catch?

2068
01:39:08,286 --> 01:39:10,220
What do you have to do?

2069
01:39:10,220 --> 01:39:12,953
I tell you these while you're playing.

2070
01:39:13,420 --> 01:39:17,453
Let's make sure you follow
the instructions for this game. Got it?

2071
01:39:17,453 --> 01:39:22,686
We're preparing well
to beat the Pink Spiders.

2072
01:39:22,686 --> 01:39:24,453
- Understood?
- Yes.

2073
01:39:25,720 --> 01:39:27,820
- Pilseung!
- Wonder Dogs!

2074
01:39:27,820 --> 01:39:30,120
(Training for the match
against the Pink Spiders)

2075
01:39:30,520 --> 01:39:33,453
The Pink Spiders hit the ball fast
on both sides.

2076
01:39:33,453 --> 01:39:35,386
So you might likely end up
with a single block.

2077
01:39:35,720 --> 01:39:38,086
The gap between blocks will be open a lot.
Go for the gap.

2078
01:39:38,286 --> 01:39:41,420
(She smoothly explains strategies.)

2079
01:39:41,820 --> 01:39:44,053
I know our opponent, more or less.

2080
01:39:44,053 --> 01:39:49,120
Playing styles or habits
of individual players.

2081
01:39:49,486 --> 01:39:51,020
Since I know many of them,

2082
01:39:51,020 --> 01:39:53,220
I may be able to give better explanations.

2083
01:39:53,586 --> 01:39:56,553
Almost all Pink Spiders players
will join the match.

2084
01:39:57,086 --> 01:40:01,853
Players like Jeong Yun Ju
and Moon Ji Yun might play.

2085
01:40:01,853 --> 01:40:04,853
Moon Ji Yun changes the line.

2086
01:40:04,853 --> 01:40:09,620
Yun Ju isn't good
at launching straight shots.

2087
01:40:09,620 --> 01:40:11,386
She tends to use cross-court spikes.

2088
01:40:11,386 --> 01:40:12,720
If the ball is fast,

2089
01:40:12,720 --> 01:40:15,620
don't spread your arms to the side.
Keep them in the middle.

2090
01:40:15,620 --> 01:40:18,653
It's important to settle blocks
at the sides.

2091
01:40:18,653 --> 01:40:21,520
Keep your positions.
Balls between your arms.

2092
01:40:21,520 --> 01:40:24,020
The Pink Spiders' hits are speedy.

2093
01:40:24,886 --> 01:40:27,420
(Under spot-on instructions,)

2094
01:40:28,353 --> 01:40:29,553
You're late!

2095
01:40:29,553 --> 01:40:31,520
(the slow Wonder Dogs are...)

2096
01:40:32,120 --> 01:40:33,953
(growing to be swift.)

2097
01:40:33,953 --> 01:40:35,753
Ball in the middle.

2098
01:40:36,120 --> 01:40:37,386
(Here comes the Pink Spiders expert.)

2099
01:40:37,386 --> 01:40:39,953
Where's the ball?

2100
01:40:39,953 --> 01:40:41,053
Jump.

2101
01:40:41,053 --> 01:40:43,753
Where's the ball?

2102
01:40:44,253 --> 01:40:47,986
Block it in the middle.

2103
01:40:47,986 --> 01:40:49,920
(Her training method is extraordinary.)

2104
01:40:49,920 --> 01:40:51,553
Keep them closer!

2105
01:40:51,553 --> 01:40:53,320
I told you to align it to the middle.

2106
01:40:53,320 --> 01:40:54,320
(Rushing)

2107
01:40:54,320 --> 01:40:56,820
(She moves in the blink of an eye.)

2108
01:40:56,820 --> 01:40:58,953
Watch out for timing. It's fast.

2109
01:40:59,661 --> 01:41:01,561
(Watching carefully)

2110
01:41:01,586 --> 01:41:02,586
Put your hands in.

2111
01:41:03,886 --> 01:41:04,920
Grab it.

2112
01:41:05,953 --> 01:41:06,953
Give it to me.

2113
01:41:07,586 --> 01:41:11,120
(A detailed individual lesson)

2114
01:41:11,120 --> 01:41:12,153
Try again.

2115
01:41:12,486 --> 01:41:13,520
Do it.

2116
01:41:14,386 --> 01:41:15,486
That's it!

2117
01:41:15,920 --> 01:41:16,986
Good.

2118
01:41:17,853 --> 01:41:18,853
Way to go.

2119
01:41:19,286 --> 01:41:20,286
It's easy.

2120
01:41:22,320 --> 01:41:24,620
It's really easy!

2121
01:41:25,053 --> 01:41:27,420
That's it. Move forward.

2122
01:41:27,420 --> 01:41:28,486
That's how you do it!

2123
01:41:29,120 --> 01:41:30,486
In the middle!

2124
01:41:30,486 --> 01:41:31,920
Okay!

2125
01:41:32,653 --> 01:41:33,686
Good.

2126
01:41:34,020 --> 01:41:35,186
Drink water.

2127
01:41:35,186 --> 01:41:37,725
- It's really hot.
- Yes. Why is it so hot today?

2128
01:41:39,353 --> 01:41:42,420
(Time for a cool, tasty drink)

2129
01:41:43,386 --> 01:41:45,253
It's refreshing to drink, like water.

2130
01:41:45,253 --> 01:41:46,253
Delicious.

2131
01:41:46,253 --> 01:41:47,286
It's like peach water.

2132
01:41:48,353 --> 01:41:49,453
Tasty.

2133
01:41:49,453 --> 01:41:50,453
It's zero sugar.

2134
01:41:50,453 --> 01:41:52,120
(They're recharged
thanks to sweet beverages.)

2135
01:41:52,320 --> 01:41:54,253
You know, I say, "One day left."

2136
01:41:54,253 --> 01:41:56,286
"Today is the last day."

2137
01:41:56,286 --> 01:41:57,786
I count deadlines, right?

2138
01:41:57,786 --> 01:42:00,053
This is not to make you nervous.

2139
01:42:00,053 --> 01:42:01,886
Since we don't have many days left now,

2140
01:42:01,886 --> 01:42:04,220
- I want you to play without regrets.
- Yes, Coach.

2141
01:42:04,220 --> 01:42:06,286
We all worked hard
to prepare for the match.

2142
01:42:06,286 --> 01:42:08,653
And we've done well and improved a lot.

2143
01:42:08,653 --> 01:42:10,720
So let's show what we've got
until the end.

2144
01:42:10,720 --> 01:42:11,753
- Got it?
- Yes.

2145
01:42:11,753 --> 01:42:12,920
All right. Let's do this.

2146
01:42:15,986 --> 01:42:17,920
- Pilseung!
- Wonder Dogs!

2147
01:42:17,920 --> 01:42:20,620
(Their final training session ends.)

2148
01:42:21,186 --> 01:42:24,153
As a head coach in the Wonder Dogs,

2149
01:42:24,153 --> 01:42:27,686
I went through many things
together with the players...

2150
01:42:27,686 --> 01:42:30,153
for a little more than two months.

2151
01:42:30,153 --> 01:42:33,686
I saw them more than during breaks.

2152
01:42:33,686 --> 01:42:38,420
We spent time together
more than we did with our families.

2153
01:42:38,953 --> 01:42:42,586
Emotionally, I believe
I've grown closer to the players...

2154
01:42:42,586 --> 01:42:44,453
as I care about them.

2155
01:42:44,453 --> 01:42:48,853
And when I reflect
that the Wonder Dogs players are...

2156
01:42:48,853 --> 01:42:55,986
my first players when I began
my career as a head coach,

2157
01:42:57,653 --> 01:43:01,153
I feel they're special to me.

2158
01:43:01,153 --> 01:43:04,386
Looking back, there were hard times.

2159
01:43:04,386 --> 01:43:07,486
But the players handled them well.

2160
01:43:07,486 --> 01:43:12,253
I think they grew stronger as a team.

2161
01:43:12,853 --> 01:43:14,286
I want the players...

2162
01:43:14,286 --> 01:43:20,420
to show what they've worked on
and improved...

2163
01:43:20,420 --> 01:43:22,553
tomorrow on the court.

2164
01:43:22,553 --> 01:43:25,020
That will be our last goal.

2165
01:43:27,020 --> 01:43:33,253
(Bangameori Beach, Ansan City)

2166
01:43:34,386 --> 01:43:36,886
(Under the orange sunset,)

2167
01:43:36,886 --> 01:43:38,520
It's so beautiful.

2168
01:43:38,520 --> 01:43:39,853
(the Wonder Dogs have come
to make their final resolution.)

2169
01:43:39,853 --> 01:43:41,186
Look at the cloud!

2170
01:43:41,186 --> 01:43:43,286
I know, right? It's so pretty.

2171
01:43:44,386 --> 01:43:45,886
I see a plane too.

2172
01:43:45,886 --> 01:43:46,953
(To capture the fleeting time,)

2173
01:43:47,253 --> 01:43:49,220
I think this is our first selfie.

2174
01:43:49,220 --> 01:43:50,753
(they take a picture.)

2175
01:43:52,886 --> 01:43:54,786
Sand is all over me!

2176
01:43:54,786 --> 01:43:56,286
It's pretty.

2177
01:44:00,786 --> 01:44:03,286
I don't think I'll forget this moment.

2178
01:44:03,286 --> 01:44:05,086
- Yes.
- That's true.

2179
01:44:05,086 --> 01:44:07,320
I'll miss you guys so much.

2180
01:44:09,586 --> 01:44:10,820
It feels weird.

2181
01:44:10,820 --> 01:44:14,853
It may be our last match tomorrow.

2182
01:44:14,853 --> 01:44:16,320
But will it really be over?

2183
01:44:16,886 --> 01:44:19,753
When would I be able to train
with my teammates again?

2184
01:44:19,753 --> 01:44:22,420
I'm a little sad,

2185
01:44:22,420 --> 01:44:23,720
but I also want to play soon.

2186
01:44:24,195 --> 01:44:26,895
When there are many people...

2187
01:44:26,920 --> 01:44:29,220
and many fans come to cheer for us,

2188
01:44:29,220 --> 01:44:31,553
I feel we can play the game better.

2189
01:44:31,553 --> 01:44:33,386
(We still have tomorrow!)

2190
01:44:33,553 --> 01:44:38,953
I wish we could all smile in the end.

2191
01:44:40,486 --> 01:44:42,220
I'm nagging you until the end!

2192
01:44:42,220 --> 01:44:43,420
(The final story of the Wonder Dogs...)

2193
01:44:45,953 --> 01:44:50,720
(made up of underdogs who were crying
at the corner of a court)

2194
01:44:53,353 --> 01:44:54,453
Who was that?

2195
01:44:55,553 --> 01:44:56,686
Pilseung!

2196
01:44:56,686 --> 01:44:59,186
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

2197
01:44:59,186 --> 01:45:02,253
(Let's show them what we've got tomorrow!)

2198
01:45:05,720 --> 01:45:07,753
(The day of the live match)

2199
01:45:10,320 --> 01:45:15,653
(Many Wonder Dogs fans came
to the stadium early in the morning.)

2200
01:45:19,086 --> 01:45:21,186
(The coffee truck that's a must
on the live match day...)

2201
01:45:21,786 --> 01:45:23,520
(is prepared by Manager Boo!)

2202
01:45:23,520 --> 01:45:24,786
("Can't the Wonder Dogs be
the eighth club?")

2203
01:45:24,786 --> 01:45:26,653
("Volleyball is really fun to watch.")

2204
01:45:26,653 --> 01:45:28,386
- Hello.
- Hello.

2205
01:45:28,386 --> 01:45:29,620
Have some coffee.

2206
01:45:30,520 --> 01:45:33,486
(You're the best, Manager Boo!)

2207
01:45:34,086 --> 01:45:36,186
(To be together for the first
and the last time,)

2208
01:45:36,953 --> 01:45:39,486
(they make their steps
from "under" to "wonder.")

2209
01:45:40,420 --> 01:45:43,153
(We're heading to the Wonder Dogs now.)

2210
01:45:43,486 --> 01:45:46,086
(Totally excited)

2211
01:45:46,586 --> 01:45:49,220
(An hour before the match)

2212
01:45:49,686 --> 01:45:52,320
(Around 2,000 seats are
gradually filling up.)

2213
01:45:52,753 --> 01:45:55,286
(Even though it's the first live game,)

2214
01:45:55,686 --> 01:45:57,020
(many volleyball fans showed interest.)

2215
01:45:57,020 --> 01:45:58,353
(Lee Yeon Jae of Suwon Special City)

2216
01:45:58,986 --> 01:46:06,086
(Thank you so much.)

2217
01:46:07,020 --> 01:46:09,486
(At that time,)

2218
01:46:09,986 --> 01:46:13,620
(today's opponent has arrived
at the stadium.)

2219
01:46:20,020 --> 01:46:22,453
(Kim Dae Kyung, the coach of Pink Spiders)

2220
01:46:23,120 --> 01:46:26,153
(Jeong Yun Ju, outside hitter)

2221
01:46:26,786 --> 01:46:30,086
(Moon Ji Yun, opposite hitter)

2222
01:46:30,586 --> 01:46:34,153
(The strongest opponent is here.)

2223
01:46:34,386 --> 01:46:36,420
(I'm here too.)

2224
01:46:37,020 --> 01:46:38,620
(Coach Kim Yeon Koung)

2225
01:46:38,620 --> 01:46:39,620
Let's go!

2226
01:46:39,917 --> 01:46:41,562
We'll be even more determined today.

2227
01:46:42,490 --> 01:46:44,923
(Her spirits are higher than usual today.)

2228
01:46:46,043 --> 01:46:46,877
Let's go.

2229
01:46:47,743 --> 01:46:48,977
For the victory

2230
01:46:48,977 --> 01:46:50,777
Good morning.

2231
01:46:51,977 --> 01:46:53,210
(Smiling)

2232
01:46:54,577 --> 01:46:55,543
Good work, everyone.

2233
01:46:57,043 --> 01:46:58,110
Do your best today.

2234
01:46:58,703 --> 01:47:00,503
You'll have a massive headache
if you lose to us.

2235
01:47:01,077 --> 01:47:02,210
(Pink Spiders players)

2236
01:47:02,210 --> 01:47:03,110
The players.

2237
01:47:04,077 --> 01:47:09,543
(We're not afraid of pro teams anymore!)

2238
01:47:10,149 --> 01:47:13,083
(Let's go and give them headaches!)

2239
01:47:13,643 --> 01:47:16,510
(Drawing attention)

2240
01:47:20,077 --> 01:47:24,943
I always played in the pink uniform.

2241
01:47:24,943 --> 01:47:27,643
The supporters sang for me
and cheered for me.

2242
01:47:28,077 --> 01:47:33,043
Now, the ones in the pink uniform
are my opponents.

2243
01:47:33,059 --> 01:47:34,339
(She'll be on the other side
of the court.)

2244
01:47:35,243 --> 01:47:39,310
(Our goal is not survival,)

2245
01:47:39,943 --> 01:47:42,243
(but to prove ourselves.)

2246
01:47:47,077 --> 01:47:49,510
(Eyes wide open)

2247
01:47:50,369 --> 01:47:52,769
(As the players enter,)

2248
01:47:56,610 --> 01:47:59,377
(the spectators cheer as loud as thunder!)

2249
01:48:00,043 --> 01:48:02,810
(It has always been quiet,)

2250
01:48:02,810 --> 01:48:08,010
(but today, the stadium is filled
with fans' cheers!)

2251
01:48:08,843 --> 01:48:11,277
(Stunned)

2252
01:48:18,877 --> 01:48:20,310
(Smiling)

2253
01:48:20,810 --> 01:48:22,943
(Na Yeon's mother-in-law, husband,
cousin, and sister)

2254
01:48:23,210 --> 01:48:25,343
The temperature
in the stadium is different...

2255
01:48:25,343 --> 01:48:27,510
when there is a crowd compared
to when it is empty.

2256
01:48:27,510 --> 01:48:29,110
Because of all the people.

2257
01:48:29,110 --> 01:48:31,010
I got goosebumps.

2258
01:48:31,910 --> 01:48:33,143
I guess I missed that.

2259
01:48:34,670 --> 01:48:36,203
I almost teared up.

2260
01:48:37,543 --> 01:48:39,843
"Right, this is where I used to play."

2261
01:48:39,868 --> 01:48:41,510
"I remember now."

2262
01:48:42,277 --> 01:48:44,177
It felt like I was dreaming.

2263
01:48:44,504 --> 01:48:47,618
I couldn't believe I was playing
in front of the huge crowd.

2264
01:48:47,643 --> 01:48:52,977
I guess I just loved
having someone cheering for us.

2265
01:48:52,977 --> 01:48:55,343
I don't know how else
to describe that feeling.

2266
01:48:56,049 --> 01:48:58,049
(Nervously looking around)

2267
01:48:59,143 --> 01:49:03,377
(She meets her fans again.)

2268
01:49:03,377 --> 01:49:05,943
(And she meets her fans
for the first time.)

2269
01:49:06,710 --> 01:49:09,810
(The players have done their part
and strived to be here.)

2270
01:49:12,523 --> 01:49:13,183
(Screaming)

2271
01:49:15,277 --> 01:49:17,610
(The cheer becomes louder!)

2272
01:49:18,743 --> 01:49:19,610
What a surprise.

2273
01:49:19,610 --> 01:49:21,043
(The newbie coach enters!)

2274
01:49:21,610 --> 01:49:25,010
(The stadium's roof is
about to blow away!)

2275
01:49:25,477 --> 01:49:29,377
(The coach is even more popular
than the team itself!)

2276
01:49:29,377 --> 01:49:30,777
(I need to capture this moment!)

2277
01:49:31,477 --> 01:49:33,477
(Kind of shy)

2278
01:49:34,343 --> 01:49:35,477
What's going on here?

2279
01:49:36,410 --> 01:49:37,310
Oh, my.
Hello.

2280
01:49:39,477 --> 01:49:42,043
I wasn't nervous at all.

2281
01:49:42,043 --> 01:49:46,443
But when I entered
and the crowd went wild,

2282
01:49:46,910 --> 01:49:49,043
I realized that this was an actual game.

2283
01:49:49,043 --> 01:49:53,010
It got me thinking, "I really have
to show them a great performance."

2284
01:49:53,010 --> 01:49:57,043
I started to worry and get nervous,

2285
01:49:57,377 --> 01:50:00,310
but in a good way.

2286
01:50:01,610 --> 01:50:05,210
(She stands on the court not as a player,
but as a coach now.)

2287
01:50:05,443 --> 01:50:08,210
The team witnessed both the beginning
and the end of the Empress.

2288
01:50:08,210 --> 01:50:11,577
It is the team that shared every moment
of Yeon Koung's...

2289
01:50:11,577 --> 01:50:14,510
twenty years of volleyball life,
with laughter and tears.

2290
01:50:14,510 --> 01:50:17,077
The newbie coach,
Yeon Koung's final opponent is...

2291
01:50:17,077 --> 01:50:21,277
Pink Spiders, the team she played for
throughout her career.

2292
01:50:21,577 --> 01:50:23,910
Today's match between Wonder Dogs
and Pink Spiders is...

2293
01:50:23,910 --> 01:50:25,510
with commentator Lee Suk Ja.

2294
01:50:25,510 --> 01:50:27,177
- Hello.
- Hello.

2295
01:50:27,177 --> 01:50:29,777
- The final opponent of Wonder Dogs is...
- Yes.

2296
01:50:29,777 --> 01:50:32,143
Pink Spiders, the strongest team
in the V-League.

2297
01:50:32,143 --> 01:50:33,210
That's right.

2298
01:50:33,210 --> 01:50:36,077
Actually, Coach Yoshihara isn't
at the court today.

2299
01:50:36,077 --> 01:50:39,810
No, she isn't, so Coach Kim Dae Kyung
will be leading the team today.

2300
01:50:39,810 --> 01:50:46,177
Coach Dae Kyung has also been close
to Coach Yeon Koung for a long time.

2301
01:50:46,177 --> 01:50:49,543
I took a look at the lineup
Coach Dae Kyung put together.

2302
01:50:49,543 --> 01:50:52,477
Many of them are top-tier players.

2303
01:50:52,477 --> 01:50:54,143
Even national team players are
on the team.

2304
01:50:54,143 --> 01:50:58,577
Exactly. Moon Ji Yun and Jeong Yun Ju,
who showed great performances...

2305
01:50:58,577 --> 01:51:00,710
on the national team,
have just joined Pink Spiders.

2306
01:51:00,710 --> 01:51:04,043
Which means they are still
in national-team form.

2307
01:51:04,043 --> 01:51:06,043
In addition, Yun Ju played the key role...

2308
01:51:06,043 --> 01:51:10,177
as Yeon Koung's partner
and led the team...

2309
01:51:10,177 --> 01:51:12,777
- to the league's victory.
- Exactly.

2310
01:51:12,777 --> 01:51:15,510
I can't wait to see what kind
of performance Wonder Dogs...

2311
01:51:15,510 --> 01:51:18,377
will show today
against such a strong team.

2312
01:51:18,377 --> 01:51:25,110
In fact, 4 out of 5 Pink Spiders
league championships were...

2313
01:51:25,110 --> 01:51:29,243
with Yeon Koung on the team.

2314
01:51:29,243 --> 01:51:31,710
That's right.
That was when she was a player.

2315
01:51:31,710 --> 01:51:34,243
Now she is not a Pink Spiders player,

2316
01:51:34,243 --> 01:51:36,677
- but the Wonder Dogs coach.
- Indeed.

2317
01:51:36,677 --> 01:51:39,077
Wonder Dogs has Yeon Koung on their side.

2318
01:51:39,077 --> 01:51:41,277
Today, we have many Pink Spiders
supporters in the audience.

2319
01:51:41,277 --> 01:51:43,743
I'm sure they are here for Pink Spiders,

2320
01:51:44,210 --> 01:51:48,843
but many of them must also be here
to support Coach Yeon Koung, right?

2321
01:51:48,843 --> 01:51:52,077
- Look at the uniforms over there.
- Right.

2322
01:51:52,077 --> 01:51:53,310
I knew this would happen.

2323
01:51:53,310 --> 01:51:56,143
- "We love Kim Yeon Koung."
- They adore her.

2324
01:51:56,143 --> 01:51:58,610
- We love her too.
- Right.

2325
01:51:58,610 --> 01:52:00,177
I saw this coming.

2326
01:52:00,843 --> 01:52:03,277
Today, we have spectators
for the first time,

2327
01:52:03,877 --> 01:52:07,643
and 2,000 fans are here.

2328
01:52:07,643 --> 01:52:11,510
I heard about 10,000 fans
applied for today's game.

2329
01:52:11,510 --> 01:52:15,143
Beating the 1 out of 5 competition,

2330
01:52:15,143 --> 01:52:16,510
only 2,000 made it in.

2331
01:52:16,510 --> 01:52:19,210
That's right. We played
against Suwon Special City.

2332
01:52:19,210 --> 01:52:21,443
- Coach Kang Min Sik is here too.
- Yes.

2333
01:52:21,443 --> 01:52:24,943
Pohang Sports Council's
Coach Kim Yoon Hye is here as well.

2334
01:52:24,943 --> 01:52:27,643
Coach Yeon Koung's parents are here too.

2335
01:52:27,643 --> 01:52:31,743
I think I have come across them
several times when she was a player.

2336
01:52:31,743 --> 01:52:34,410
But today, they are here
to support the coach.

2337
01:52:34,410 --> 01:52:35,270
They must be wondering...

2338
01:52:35,294 --> 01:52:37,110
whether their daughter would fit
as a coach too.

2339
01:52:37,110 --> 01:52:38,843
They must be wondering whether their
daughter would fit as a coach, too.

2340
01:52:38,843 --> 01:52:41,843
So far, Wonder Dogs players
have always played...

2341
01:52:41,843 --> 01:52:44,643
surrounded by the opponents' supporters.

2342
01:52:44,643 --> 01:52:45,643
That's right.

2343
01:52:48,510 --> 01:52:51,177
(The pro team supporters' vibrant cheer)

2344
01:52:51,777 --> 01:52:54,277
(Next to them, Wonder Dogs' families
seemed somewhat lonely.)

2345
01:52:56,877 --> 01:53:00,777
(Shujitsu High School's supporters' cheer
left a strong impression.)

2346
01:53:03,410 --> 01:53:04,977
(Sometimes, their ex-teams' cheer...)

2347
01:53:04,977 --> 01:53:06,743
(made them dizzy.)

2348
01:53:07,677 --> 01:53:10,810
(But today, it's different.)

2349
01:53:10,810 --> 01:53:11,710
(Won...)
(Der...)

2350
01:53:12,543 --> 01:53:13,477
(Dogs)

2351
01:53:13,477 --> 01:53:14,877
Applause!

2352
01:53:14,877 --> 01:53:17,343
(Their reliable fans are here
for the first time!)

2353
01:53:17,343 --> 01:53:20,010
Today, this new setting could
be exciting for them...

2354
01:53:20,010 --> 01:53:22,477
or make them awkward and nervous too.

2355
01:53:22,477 --> 01:53:24,243
Right. It can motivate them,

2356
01:53:24,243 --> 01:53:26,710
- but it can also make them nervous.
- Right.

2357
01:53:27,677 --> 01:53:30,110
(Let's keep on cheering them!)

2358
01:53:30,643 --> 01:53:31,977
(Starting from Captain Pyo...)

2359
01:53:32,002 --> 01:53:33,835
- Pyo Seung Ju!
- Pyo Seung Ju!

2360
01:53:34,277 --> 01:53:35,677
(Following the cheerleader...)

2361
01:53:35,677 --> 01:53:36,510
Faster!

2362
01:53:36,510 --> 01:53:37,577
- Enkhsoyol!
- Enkhsoyol!

2363
01:53:37,577 --> 01:53:39,410
(Enkhsoyol, baby boy)

2364
01:53:39,410 --> 01:53:40,217
Faster!

2365
01:53:40,241 --> 01:53:41,343
- Enkhsoyol!
- Enkhsoyol!

2366
01:53:41,743 --> 01:53:44,443
(This time,
always high-spirited Myoung Hwa!)

2367
01:53:44,777 --> 01:53:47,977
(Even the supporters got high-spirited.)

2368
01:53:48,377 --> 01:53:49,277
(Very nice! Na Hee is the best!)

2369
01:53:49,277 --> 01:53:51,977
- Kim Na Hee!
- Kim Na Hee!

2370
01:53:52,477 --> 01:53:55,910
(The audience is warmed up,
calling the players!)

2371
01:53:55,910 --> 01:53:59,010
Pink Spiders cannot be mentioned
without Coach Yeon Koung,

2372
01:53:59,010 --> 01:54:01,010
and this player too.

2373
01:54:01,010 --> 01:54:03,810
She is Pink Spiders' one-club player,

2374
01:54:03,810 --> 01:54:04,910
- Kim Na Hee.
- Right.

2375
01:54:04,910 --> 01:54:07,643
She's always been
Pink Spiders' Number Seven.

2376
01:54:07,643 --> 01:54:10,510
For 17 years,
she never changed her number.

2377
01:54:10,510 --> 01:54:13,210
Number Seven was always hers.

2378
01:54:13,210 --> 01:54:16,377
Now, she is Number Seven on Wonder Dogs.

2379
01:54:16,377 --> 01:54:20,343
On Pink Spiders,
Choi Eun Ji is Number Seven.

2380
01:54:20,343 --> 01:54:24,243
Eun Ji is the captain
of Pink Spiders today,

2381
01:54:24,243 --> 01:54:26,677
and her number is seven.

2382
01:54:26,677 --> 01:54:29,110
- Will the original Number Seven...
- The original Number Seven,

2383
01:54:29,110 --> 01:54:32,443
- will she show a great performance today?
- Yes.

2384
01:54:32,443 --> 01:54:34,343
As far as I see,

2385
01:54:34,343 --> 01:54:37,577
Wonder Dogs have already transformed
from underdogs to Wonder Dogs.

2386
01:54:37,577 --> 01:54:39,310
My last hope is for Wonder Dogs...

2387
01:54:39,310 --> 01:54:41,177
to finish their final match
wonderfully today.

2388
01:54:41,177 --> 01:54:42,943
- You have come prepared, right?
- Yes.

2389
01:54:43,410 --> 01:54:47,443
For a wonderful finale for Wonder Dogs,

2390
01:54:47,443 --> 01:54:51,110
I hope they emerge victorious today.

2391
01:54:52,043 --> 01:54:56,010
We'll focus early in the game today.

2392
01:54:56,010 --> 01:54:58,410
Seung Ju, Enkhsoyol,

2393
01:54:58,877 --> 01:54:59,877
Myoung Hwa, Hyeon Jeong,

2394
01:55:00,977 --> 01:55:03,077
Na Yeon, Song Hee, and Hye In. Okay?

2395
01:55:03,077 --> 01:55:04,010
Yes.
Okay.

2396
01:55:04,752 --> 01:55:07,018
- Pilseung!
- Wonder Dogs!

2397
01:55:07,043 --> 01:55:09,243
(Let's get them early in the game!)

2398
01:55:12,843 --> 01:55:15,443
Their pipes are not in sync,
so watch out for the tips.

2399
01:55:16,977 --> 01:55:19,043
(Let's show what champions look like!)

2400
01:55:22,510 --> 01:55:25,143
Now, the players will be introduced.

2401
01:55:25,443 --> 01:55:27,443
(The light goes off.)

2402
01:55:27,743 --> 01:55:30,643
Let me introduce...

2403
01:55:30,643 --> 01:55:33,410
Pilseung Wonder Dogs!

2404
01:55:33,410 --> 01:55:36,577
(Let's go, Wonder Dogs!)

2405
01:55:41,077 --> 01:55:43,577
(World Champion, the Empress
of Volleyball, Kim Yeon Koung)

2406
01:55:44,243 --> 01:55:46,777
(Her new challenge as a coach!)

2407
01:55:49,477 --> 01:55:53,443
(Excitement goes up to the maximum!)

2408
01:55:57,077 --> 01:55:59,443
The leader of Pilseung Wonder Dogs,

2409
01:55:59,443 --> 01:56:03,777
Coach Kim Yeon Koung!

2410
01:56:09,810 --> 01:56:12,543
(In front of 2,000 fans,)

2411
01:56:13,143 --> 01:56:16,210
(it's time for Yeon Koung
to prove herself as a coach!)

2412
01:56:27,610 --> 01:56:29,677
(Pink Spiders' player Kim Yeon Koung)

2413
01:56:30,877 --> 01:56:32,877
Today, we are playing at home.

2414
01:56:33,210 --> 01:56:34,843
We can never go easy on them.

2415
01:56:35,277 --> 01:56:37,510
We will dominate the court today.

2416
01:56:38,602 --> 01:56:41,171
I'd really love to win
since the audience will be here.

2417
01:56:41,172 --> 01:56:43,508
(The one and only match
open to the public)

2418
01:56:43,975 --> 01:56:46,477
(We can't let our fans down.)

2419
01:56:47,545 --> 01:56:50,515
(But the opponent is
the pro league champion.)

2420
01:56:54,485 --> 01:56:55,886
Are you kidding me right now?

2421
01:56:56,487 --> 01:56:58,422
You think this is a joke?

2422
01:56:58,656 --> 01:57:00,791
(Did they make a huge mistake?)

2423
01:57:01,392 --> 01:57:04,595
(But then, they hear their names
chanted in the air.)

2424
01:57:04,595 --> 01:57:06,197
- Pyo Seung Ju!
- Pyo Seung Ju!

2425
01:57:06,197 --> 01:57:08,199
- Yoon Young In!
- Yoon Young In!

2426
01:57:08,232 --> 01:57:10,745
(It's time to answer those cheers.)

2427
01:57:10,770 --> 01:57:12,090
I guess it woke me up.

2428
01:57:12,336 --> 01:57:13,504
We can do this!

2429
01:57:13,504 --> 01:57:16,307
We need scores! Let's just win three.

2430
01:57:16,307 --> 01:57:17,375
(Bring it.)

2431
01:57:21,044 --> 01:57:23,446
(We are...)

2432
01:57:24,650 --> 01:57:28,587
(the strongest when we're together.)

2433
01:57:29,355 --> 01:57:32,124
(Now it's time to bring this journey
to its end.)

2434
01:57:32,424 --> 01:57:34,192
(From underdogs...)

2435
01:57:34,193 --> 01:57:35,194
(to Wonder Dogs)

2436
01:57:36,929 --> 01:57:38,387
(The Wonder Coach)
